90, 180, and counterclockwise 90.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/22/code.py:31:#   Old logic: search for an L-shaped color with count 3, derive a corner, then test many\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/15/code.py:23:#    - Here: a structure first reads its tooth color and its opening direction from geometry.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/15/code.py:49:#      ray is only used to infer the opening direction and slot stack; color performs the match.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/15/code.py:220:    - Read each structure's tooth color and opening direction from its geometry.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/1/code.py:511:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Build L-shaped arm waypoints for _path_crossing_all / _path_through.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/1/code.py:10:#    In this combo, the output core is a non-rectangular connected shape (mostly L-shapes, plus\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/1/code.py:19:#    Small example: for a top+left target on an L-shape, the old logic would ask whether the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:25:#      a centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp of that glyph.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:65:#    - The center overwrite assumes maroon can be painted on top of either lattice color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:79:#      black/orange periodic lattice everywhere, plus a maroon 2x2 stamp only in the centered\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:83:#      for the direct glyph-derived phase cells, and maroon for the center stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:167:    Reinterpret the colored 3x3 contour glyph as a directly copied phase mask, invert the lattice color roles, and stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:177:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 into the centered 6x6 region and recolor the glyph pixels to maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:19:#        2. tile the 3x3 glyph 2x2 into a 6x6 maroon center stamp\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:22:#        2. the maroon glyph is moved to exactly one corner, chosen by glyph type\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:24:#        source: decode plus -> lattice -> 6x6 maroon plus-tiling at rows/cols 5..10\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:26:#                place one 3x3 maroon plus at the top-left corner\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:45:#    - The fused rule therefore uses a single 3x3 maroon glyph in one corner. This\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:58:#        2. exactly one corner contains the maroon glyph, and which corner it is varies\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:67:#        maroon overwrite only in one 3x3 corner.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:72:#    - The output uses only black, orange, and maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:149:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice with a black center void and a glyph-specific maroon corner stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:159:    - Overwrite the centered 6x6 area with pure black, then place one maroon 3x3 copy of the glyph into the corner assigned to that glyph class.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:162:    - The input contour now controls two output attributes at once: it still determines the orange lattice phase, and it also selects which corner receives the only maroon glyph while the center stays empty.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:224:    maroon_corners = [name for name, view in corner_views.items() if np.any(view == Color.MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:225:    if maroon_corners != [glyph_name]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/9/code.py:297:    - Recover every structure's opening direction and tooth-gap span from its solid back wall and spaced teeth.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D6/0/code.py:487:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Build L-shaped arm waypoints for _path_crossing_all / _path_through.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/9/code.py:24:#     - output stays a 16x16 orange/black period-3 lattice with a centered 6x6 maroon overlay\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/9/code.py:83:#     - the output still uses only black, orange, and maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/9/code.py:150:    Treat the colored 3x3 asymmetric glyph as an oriented phase code, then render a mirrored maroon stamp at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/9/code.py:161:    - In the centered 6x6 region, place four transformed maroon copies of the glyph: original, horizontal flip, vertical flip, and 180-degree rotation.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:24:#     - output stays a 16x16 black/orange period-3 lattice with a centered 6x6 maroon stamp\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:38:#       4. tile the rotated phase across 16x16, then stamp the observed 111/100/100 motif in maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:58:#     - the centered 6x6 maroon stamp is unchanged and safely overwrites the tiled lattice last\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:60:#     - a human sees the oriented glyph twice: once in the input and again as the 2x2 maroon stamp\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:66:#     - only three colors appear in the output: black, orange, maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:167:    - Repeat the rotated phase tile over the 16x16 black canvas, then tile the observed motif 2x2 and recolor its true cells to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/29/code.py:35:#      maroon and still mean \\\"go left 4\\\"; therefore the solver must decode motion from shape only.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/19/code.py:211:    - For every structure, read its opening direction from the tooth geometry and read its target color from the wall color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D14/0/code.py:513:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Build L-shaped arm waypoints for _path_crossing_all / _path_through.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:22:#    repeat one orange/black lattice -> stamp that glyph in maroon at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:31:#    the earlier one on shared cells. The center stamp stays a single 2x2 maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:59:#    The output still uses only black, two layer colors, and one centered maroon stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:178:    Decode two colored copies of the same contour glyph into shifted lattice layers, then place the shared glyph as a centered maroon seal.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:188:    - Composite the two shifted lattices so the later bbox in row-major order overwrites the earlier one on overlap, then stamp the shared glyph tiled 2x2 in maroon inside the centered 6x6 window.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/15/code.py:24:#    whole column and returned the dense rectangle. Here the source core is an L-shape: think\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/15/code.py:27:#    silhouette of that L-shape rather than spanning an entire row/column. Example: if the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/15/code.py:32:#    L-shaped core canvas -> erase the dominant non-background fill color to 0. The result is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/15/code.py:35:#    The generator deliberately stays with one irregular family: a single corner-notch L-shape.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:17:#   output still consists of a tiled orange/black phase lattice plus a centered 2x2 maroon stamp\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:51:#   comfortably larger than the fixed 6x6 maroon stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:57:# - Foreground color is chosen from the same safe set excluding black, orange, and maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:69:#   maroon stamp. No extra markers are added.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:75:#   color, while the output still uses only black, orange, and maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:139:    - Tile the phase tile across that canvas, then place a centered 6x6 maroon stamp made by 2x2 tiling of the original glyph.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/25/code.py:50:#       - Suppose the frame contains three slots: a unit cell, a domino, and an L-shape.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D15/1/code.py:80:#   - main() assumes marker components are color-5 L-shapes of area 3. The\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:26:#   - a maroon stamp is always the 2x2 tiling of the 3x3 glyph, so each stamp is 6x6\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:36:#     - output gets one centered 6x6 maroon stamp at (5, 5)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:62:#   - maroon stamps are large and repeated, making the regular spacing easy to see\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:156:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice and stamp a shifted 2x2 maroon stamp array.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:166:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 to form a 6x6 maroon stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:170:    - The glyph carries two independent visible signals: its shape still determines the orange phase lattice, while its input position now controls the global offset of an evenly spaced four-stamp maroon array.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/13/code.py:323:    - Ray-cast outward from each structure's interior socket cells and collect the red components visible on each opening direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/5/code.py:148:    Decode the 3x3 contour cue into the original 16x16 periodic lattice, then stamp a mixed-symmetry 2x2 arrangement of that glyph in maroon at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/5/code.py:158:    - In the centered 6x6 window, place four 3x3 maroon copies of the glyph using a mixed D4 layout:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/8/code.py:26:#    - D3/1 breaks the old color-shape binding: a plus may be orange, teal, maroon, etc.,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/8/code.py:31:#        glyphs in reading order = cross(teal), plus(maroon), diamond(teal), plus(orange)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D9/0/code.py:24:#    - Old logic: three L-shaped sprites outside = red, red, blue ->\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D9/0/code.py:25:#      every L-shaped hole becomes solid red.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D9/0/code.py:26:#    - New logic: three L-shaped sprites outside = pattern A, pattern A,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D9/0/code.py:27:#      pattern B -> every L-shaped hole receives the aligned copy of pattern A.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/22/code.py:21:#    candidate slots, each with the same opening direction but its own exact\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/22/code.py:55:#    structure opening direction, so motion is axis-aligned and stays faithful to\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/22/code.py:355:    - Parse each comb into individual per-tooth docking lanes inside the cavity, recovering both the opening direction and the exact rectangle shape for each lane.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:27:#   4. Put a centered 6x6 maroon stamp made from a plain 2x2 copy of the input glyph.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:39:#   by one row, and the centered maroon stamp is built from mirrored copies of the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:69:# - Inside the center, maroon is the only overlay color and stays confined to one\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:184:    Decode one colored 3x3 contour glyph into a color-transferred phase lattice, then place a mirrored maroon stamp at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:195:    - Repeat the colored phase seed over the 16x16 black canvas, then place a centered 6x6 maroon mirror-collage\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/31/code.py:22:#   - 本融合版：例如某个 L 形槽位在框内右上角是红格；对应输入精灵先以另一朝向散落在外部，且红点落在其某个块的右上角。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/31/code.py:23:#     这个右上角不是目标位置，而是“旋转说明书”。solver 必须先解码为“旋转 180 度”，在块级把 L 形和标记格一起转正，\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/34/code.py:34:#   the maroon center stamp and the orange/black lattice both rotate together.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/34/code.py:59:#   The output still uses the original three-color palette (black, orange, maroon), so the new\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/34/code.py:175:    - Build the same 16x16 orange/black lattice and centered 2x2 maroon stamp as the canonical family would produce, then rotate the entire finished canvas by the recovered quarter-turn.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:18:#       color: any single color except black(0), grey(5), orange(7), maroon(9)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:23:#     stamp: the original 4x4 motif tiled 2x2 into a centered 8x8 maroon block\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:24:#     colors_used: black(0), grey(5), orange(7), maroon(9)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:75:#    - The centered maroon stamp exposes the exact 4x4 motif geometry, giving the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:87:#      maroon for the stamp. The third lattice color always comes from the same logical\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:196:    Read a 4x4 contour code, expand it into a period-4 tricolor lattice, and stamp a centered maroon 2x2 copy of the motif.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:206:    - Repeat that 4x4 tricolor tile over a 16x16 canvas, then place a 2x2 maroon tiling of the original motif in the centered 8x8 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/37/code.py:31:    - each control is now a 3-cell L-shaped arrow touching exactly one border:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/37/code.py:64:    ctrl components, requires size-3 2x2 L-shapes, and decodes one launch site per\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/37/code.py:104:  - All ctrl cells belong to 1 or 2 size-3 L-shaped arrow components.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/12/code.py:382:    - Parse each structure to recover its opening direction and the exact dock rectangle implied by the teeth.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:17:#      output is still 16x16 and still ends with a centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp of that glyph.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:22:#      3. The maroon stamp is written last on top.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:38:#      stamps the 6x6 maroon H pattern. The center region therefore has two visible rhythms.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:61:#    - Original final maroon overwrite remains valid and must still happen last.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:68:#    - The detail window is fixed to rows/cols 3..12 and the 6x6 maroon stamp sits at rows/cols\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:81:#      overlay, maroon stamp. The two tiled layers share the same orange/black palette and combine\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:90:#      maroon stamp copied from the input glyph.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:226:    Decode one 3x3 contour glyph into a two-scale tiled scene whose background and center detail use different period tables, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:236:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon inside the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D5/1/code.py:26:#   complementary shape: its color is offset by how many maroon 9-rectangles the routed wire passes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D5/1/code.py:279:      color is increased by the number of maroon 9-rectangles that path passes through.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/24/code.py:12:# - Concrete behavior shift: if frame A contains an L-shaped hole and frame B a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:20:#      into a 6x6 maroon stamp -> place that stamp at the fixed centered box\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:24:#      3x3 into a 9x9 maroon stamp -> aim for the geometric center first, then snap\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:30:#      snaps that to the nearest period-3 boundary, namely (3,3). The final maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:35:#      lattice decoding. This keeps the task readable while making the maroon region\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:62:#      the intended maroon-over-lattice overwrite already present in the base task.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:67:#    - The maroon area becomes both larger and shifted relative to naive centering.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:75:#    - The output still has only three colors: black, orange, and maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:178:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a periodic 16x16 lattice, then overlay a larger maroon stamp snapped to the lattice grid.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:188:    - Tile the original glyph 3x3 to build a 9x9 stamp, recolor its True pixels to maroon, and place it at the nearest legal 3x3 tile boundary rather than at the old fixed center box.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:191:    - The contour still determines the lattice phase, but the stamp geometry is now governed by two coupled constraints: it is larger because of 3x3 tiling, and it must sit on the lattice's own 3x3 boundary system, so the maroon region lands as a clean 3-by-3 block of tiles.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:33:#      phase pattern of the decoded glyph. The centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:70:#      maroon center stamp still anchors the correspondence to the input glyph.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:76:#      the maroon center stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:79:#      maroon keeps its center-stamp role, and the input's two non-orange colors\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:212:    Recover a 3x3 contour glyph from a textured 6x6 board, then render its decoded lattice with thicker black grid lines and the usual centered maroon stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:222:    - Tile that 4x4 carrier across the 16x16 output and place a 2x2 maroon tiling of the recovered glyph in the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/28/code.py:13:#    1-pixel L-shaped trail colored with that object's dominant fill color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/3/code.py:20:#      either L to fit either L-shaped hole. The fused logic is stricter: the two L pieces are only\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:24:    - 原题从目标 3x3 块外的可通行格做普通 BFS，把所有可达 maroon 按步数远近搬回目标块。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:25:      例如某个 maroon 离入口 4 步、另一个 6 步，那么 4 步的先进入目标，即使那条路一直贴着墙走。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:26:    - 融合后仍然只允许沿 orange/maroon 的 4 连通路径到达，但“距离”不再是步数，而是：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:28:    - 具体小例子：一枚 maroon 在入口旁边的 2 格死胡同里，路径两格都被三面墙夹住，总代价可能是\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:29:      3 + 3 = 6；另一枚更远的 maroon 在较宽主通道深处，沿路 5 格每格只贴 1 面墙，总代价只有 5。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:44:    - 原 main() 依赖“可达 maroon 数 = 要填入目标的数量”。这一点仍保留，所以生成器只放 k 个可达\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:45:      maroon，其余 maroon 全都放在隔离口袋里做 distractor。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:47:    - 目标块固定在 11x11 的中心 3x3；除目标块外，其余单元只会是 floor、wall 或 maroon。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:51:    - 人类可以直接看到：有些 maroon 虽然步数更近，但卡在三面贴墙的死胡同；另一些更远，却位于\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:53:    - 由于目标块仍按 row-major 填入，观察者只需比较“哪些 maroon 消失了”，就能对照迷宫几何推断\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:56:    - 场景仍只有五种颜色，且各自语义稳定：orange 地板、magenta 墙、green/red 目标、maroon token。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:423:    Move the reachable maroon pixels with the smallest wall-contact path cost into the centered 3x3 target block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:427:    - Orange cells are walkable floor, magenta cells are maze walls, and maroon cells sit on floor cells inside the maze.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:430:    - Start from every floor/maroon cell directly adjacent to the destination block and traverse only floor or maroon cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:432:    - Keep only reachable maroon pixels, rank them by this accumulated wall-neighbor cost, and place the closest ones into the destination in row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:433:    - Any maroon that moves is erased from its source cell and replaced by orange floor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:435:    Key insight: In the maze, the winning maroons are not always the fewest steps away; wider passages can beat shorter but tighter dead ends because distance is driven by repeated contact with nearby walls.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:454:    maroons = [(int(expo[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:455:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < inf]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:456:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:459:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:460:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/34/code.py:15:#    - The source core is now a non-rectangular L-shape: a filled rectangle with the corner opposite the control\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/34/code.py:28:#    - I use one non-rectangular family (L-shape) rather than mixing many silhouettes. That keeps the puzzle readable\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/34/code.py:47:#    - The center object visibly has an L-shaped dense region, not a plain rectangle.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/34/code.py:48:#    - Outputs are sparse rather than dense, and their occupied colored cells still spread across the L-shape, so the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/11/code.py:38:      - 假设某个 slot 是 3 格 L 形，k=3\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/5/code.py:9:#    - Each corridor color receives a same-color 2x2 L-shaped legend glyph:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:15:#      sorts reachable maroons by flood-fill distance.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:19:#    - Sorting is intentionally decoupled from that path wave: once maroons are known to\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:28:#      maroons; otherwise \\\"sorting\\\" would be invisible because every reachable token would\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:38:#    - Erasing moved maroons back to floor=7 remains valid because the spec keeps the same\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:41:#    - Walls, destination, source maroons, and sealed distractor pockets are placed on\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:47:#    - The output retains some outside maroons because only nine move; this exposes which\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:126:def _reachable_maroons(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:129:    maroons: list[tuple[int, int, int]] = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:132:            maroons.append((_euclid2(int(r), int(c), cr, cc), int(r), int(c)))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:133:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:134:    return maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:152:    Pull the Euclidean-closest reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:155:    - Orange floor holds scattered maroon tokens, magenta wall cells, and one fixed 3x3 target block whose center is the unique red pixel.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:159:    - Start from every floor/maroon cell that touches the target block in 8-neighbor sense, then flood-fill through floor+maroon with 8-connectivity; this is the reachability test and its path metric is Chebyshev-style 8-step BFS.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:160:    - Keep only maroon pixels reached by that wave, but rank them by Euclidean distance to the red center rather than by flood-fill distance; ties break by row then column.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:161:    - Move the best k=min(9, reachable_count) maroons into the destination block in row-major order and erase those source cells back to orange floor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:177:    ranked = _reachable_maroons(grid, dist8, cr, cc)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D16/2/code.py:36:#       stage_2: \\\"fill every L-shaped hole with yellow, not red\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D9/3/code.py:36:#       avoids covering crossings or maroon junction rectangles.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/7/code.py:53:      suppose a slot is an L-shape:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:9:#      scattered maroon tokens outside the block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:11:#      ranked reachable maroons by increasing BFS distance, and wrote them into\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:14:#      1. Candidate maroons are ranked from far to near.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:26:#      added. With identical maroon tokens, D3 only changes the output when more\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:42:#    - The old `k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))` also breaks because the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:45:#      set should be erased; the extra near maroons must survive in place.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:50:#    - Source and distractor maroons are sampled only from floor cells outside\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:57:#      effects co-occur: far maroons disappear while near ones remain, the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:70:#      maroon moves, floor is restored, green stays as empty target cells, and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:199:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:200:    maroons = [triple for triple in maroons if triple[0] < 10**9]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:201:    return dest_cells, fill_order, center, floor, maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:206:    Move the farthest reachable maroon pixels into the destination block while leaving the red center untouched.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:209:    - The board is an orange floor with optional magenta wall barriers and scattered maroon source pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:213:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells touching the target, walking only through floor or maroon cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:214:    - Reachable maroon pixels are ranked from farthest to nearest by BFS distance, with row/column tie-breaks.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:215:    - The chosen maroons are erased from their source positions and copied into the target in reverse row-major order starting from the lower-right, but the red center cell is always skipped.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:223:    dest_cells, fill_order, _center, floor, maroons = _analyze_grid(grid)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:225:    maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:226:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:227:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:444:    dest_cells, fill_order, center, floor, maroons = _analyze_grid(inp)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:445:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:446:    ordered_far = sorted(maroons, key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:447:    ordered_near = sorted(maroons)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:471:        \\\"reachable_count\\\": len(maroons),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D3/0/code.py:14:#       red L-shape x5, green L-shape x1\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:92:#    - Turns keep the original L-shape vocabulary, so the scene stays readable:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:7:#   A canonical corridor sits beside the 3x3 destination block. The first maroon is within\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:9:#   them, and the fourth remains at distance 4 even after earlier maroons disappear. This\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:15:#   In the base task maroon cells were globally passable, so deleting one could not shorten any\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:16:#   route. Here only orange floor is traversable; a maroon may be used only as the final target\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:23:#   Walls isolate one narrow chamber, so a human can see the front maroon disappear first,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:24:#   then notice that deeper maroons become newly available one by one. The untouched fourth\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:25:#   maroon demonstrates the path-length threshold.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:28:#   1. at least one maroon is collected by the fused solver,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:29:#   2. at least two collected maroons were not initially eligible under the threshold,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:30:#   3. an iterative solver without the threshold would collect strictly more maroons.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:289:    Pull maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center, one shortest-path step at a time.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:297:    - Repeatedly recompute which maroon pixel is reachable from the destination through orange floor cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:298:    - A maroon qualifies only if its current shortest path length is at most 3, where the last step may enter the maroon but other maroons are not traversable.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:299:    - On each iteration, move only the single nearest qualifying maroon into the next destination cell in row-major order, erase its source to floor, then recompute from the updated grid.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:300:    - Stop when the block is full or no maroon remains within the path-length limit.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:303:    - Removing one maroon can open a shorter route to deeper maroons, so the reachable set is dynamic; however the 3-step cap still prevents some connected maroons from ever being collected.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/19/code.py:42:#    cyan/maroon pixels. Across examples, that local divider cue flips whether the first\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D12/0/code.py:24:#    means pink, pink, orange; a teal source means teal, teal, maroon; a green source\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D12/0/code.py:71:    8: 9,  # teal -> maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/0/code.py:43:#    - 仍保留大部分 8 号竖线和少量 5 号普通直穿标记；9 号块只替换少数关键交叉，不让整张图变成大块 maroon 噪声。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/0/code.py:282:    Route endpoint tokens through pipe networks whose maroon rectangles act as quarter-turn mirrors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D3/1/code.py:41:#       - Suppose a hole has L-shape.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D3/1/code.py:42:#       - Outside sprites include L-shapes in red, red, yellow.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D3/1/code.py:46:#       - The same L-shape hole now only has, for example, blue L-sprites outside.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D3/1/code.py:47:#       - The new solver records \\\"L-shape -> blue\\\" directly and fills all matching\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:54:    - 真实竖直转弯和假陷阱入口都使用统一的 L 形几何, 视觉上容易并排比较.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/43/code.py:174:    - A magenta rectangular frame surrounds that block; some non-corner frame cells are replaced by maroon markers, and some frame cells are removed as 1-pixel openings.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/43/code.py:178:    - A maroon frame marker is collectible only if the flood can touch it from the outside of the rectangle through one of the frame openings.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D5/2/code.py:36:     legend piece, generation keeps a geometrically distinctive L-shaped anchor piece and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D5/2/code.py:411:LEGEND_THRESHOLD = {8: 4, 10: 5, 12: 9}        # min extent threshold per side for anchor L-shape\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D5/2/code.py:413:LEGEND_ARM_RANGE = range(1, 4)                 # arm width/height options for L-shape construction\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D5/2/code.py:464:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Build an L-shaped anchor piece mask anchored at (0,0) of the side*side grid.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/35/code.py:32:    - 两个面积 5 的 slot 形状不同，左上的是真 L 形，右下的是横条。外部真实 piece 的摆放顺序被反过来，\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/35/code.py:33:      因此按面积排序后，同面积 tie-break 会把“横条 piece”先贴到“L 形 slot”的位置。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:234:    - The background is the dominant color. Other cells form cyan wires, optional maroon rectangular junction blocks, and colored 3x3 tokens positioned two cells away from wire endpoints.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:15:#   In the original task, if six reachable maroon tokens are ranked closest first,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:18:#   so a cropped view of the old output would contain a maroon center once k >= 5.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:36:#   destination block and that at least one adjacent floor/maroon cell exists to seed\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:41:#   Source maroons are sampled only from reachable floor cells outside the 3x3 block;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:47:#   maroons around it, making the \\\"skip center\\\" rule visible in 2-4 examples.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:49:#   The cropped output contains only green, red, and maroon inside one 3x3 block, so\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:94:def _rank_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:146:    ranked = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:155:    - The full 11x11 scene still contains orange floor, optional magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and one green 3x3 target block around a unique red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:159:    - Flood-fill from passable cells adjacent to the target through orange and maroon cells, ignoring magenta walls.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:160:    - Sort reachable maroon tokens by BFS distance, then by row and column.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:164:    Key insight: The outside world is still needed to decide how many maroons qualify, but the returned grid is only the cropped destination state, with the center acting as a fixed reference point.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:167:    ranked = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D17/1/code.py:13:#   Original logic: if an L-shaped hole had outside L sprites in red/red/green, the solver counted colors\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/32/code.py:18:#      two L-shaped holes belong to the same D4 family but face different directions. In the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:18:#    - The original task does one static BFS, sorts every reachable maroon once, then fills the 3x3 target.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:19:#    - This combo turns the wall into a local crumble mechanic: when a maroon is collected, every magenta wall\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:23:#         2. Take only the currently nearest reachable maroon layer.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:29:#    - Only two dynamic gates are used, but each sample contains multiple layers and 5-8 collected maroons.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:31:#    - The layout varies by optional filler maroons and grid rotation/flip, which keeps samples from looking cloned\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:36:#    - A collected maroon may alter the obstacle map, so the solver must mutate a working copy of the grid.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:37:#    - The generator must keep trigger maroons near only their intended gates; otherwise 3x3 crumble would open\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:52:#    - The total collectible maroons stay within 9, so every moved maroon has a destination cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:53:#    - Trigger maroons are spaced so that their 3x3 crumble neighborhoods do not accidentally merge unrelated gates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:77:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Distance from the destination-adjacent frontier through floor/maroon cells; adjacent cells start at 1.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:107:    - final_work: grid after maroons are erased and dynamic walls have crumbled\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:108:    - collected: maroons collected in layer order, row-major inside each layer\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:165:def _static_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:166:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Reachable maroons under the original static-wall interpretation, used only for generator validation/metrics.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:168:    maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON) if (r, c) not in DEST_SET and dist[r, c] > 0]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:169:    maroons.sort(key=lambda rc: (int(dist[rc[0], rc[1]]), rc[0], rc[1]))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:170:    return maroons[:DEST_LIMIT]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:175:    Move maroons into the target block by repeatedly taking the current BFS-nearest layer and crumbling nearby walls.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:178:    - The grid is 11x11 with an orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and a fixed 3x3 green target\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:180:    - Some maroons sit in rooms that are initially sealed by magenta barriers, while earlier reachable maroons sit next\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:184:    - Run BFS from floor/maroon cells adjacent to the target, but collect only the nearest reachable maroon layer.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:185:    - After collecting that layer, erase those maroons to floor and turn every wall in each collected maroon's 3x3\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:187:    - Continue until no more maroons are reachable; place the collected maroons into the target block in row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:252:    # Hall / room floors remain orange by default. Mark fixed and optional maroons.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:279:    static_reachable = _static_reachable_maroons(inp)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/14/code.py:66:- New combo-specific assumption: once the correct transform is chosen, the guide geometry is a clean L-shape\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/41/code.py:48:#      for each corridor color, a same-color 2x2 L-shape encodes the global turn\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/41/code.py:264:    - The bottom 2 rows are a legend band made of same-color 2x2 L-shapes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/2/code.py:309:    - Background cells surround orthogonal wire networks, optional maroon 9-rect pass-through blocks,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/45/code.py:16:#    - The original task sorted every reachable maroon token individually by\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/45/code.py:27:#      distance 1: [(6,5,maroon)] -> output cell maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/45/code.py:29:#      The destination begins [grey, maroon, blue, ...] in row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/45/code.py:34:#      maroon}. Each sample uses only 2-3 of them, so mixed layers are visible\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D2/3/code.py:356:LEGEND_THRESHOLD = {8: 4, 10: 5, 12: 9}       # min extent threshold per side for legend L-shape\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D2/3/code.py:358:LEGEND_ARM_RANGE = range(1, 4)                 # arm width/height options for L-shape construction\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D2/3/code.py:404:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Build an L-shaped legend piece mask anchored at (0,0) of the side*side grid.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D12/1/code.py:28:#      old rule: L-shaped hole + outside L sprites in red/red/green -> fill red by plurality.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D12/1/code.py:29:#      new rule: L-shaped hole + outside L sprites all red -> fill red directly.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:33:#    - 原来的 `maroons.sort()` 默认是 `(flood_distance,row,col)`; 融合后必须改成\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:36:#    - 原 solver 里“k = min(9, reachable_maroon_count)”仍成立; 新 generator 明确围绕这个容量上限造样例。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:145:def _reachable_maroons(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:151:    maroons = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:155:            maroons.append((rr, cc))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:156:    return maroons, dist\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:181:    maroons, dist = _reachable_maroons(grid, center)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:183:        source_order = _sort_sources_combo(maroons, center)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:185:        source_order = _sort_sources_legacy(maroons, dist)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:212:    maroons, dist = _reachable_maroons(grid, center)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:213:    combo_sources = _sort_sources_combo(maroons, center)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:214:    legacy_sources = _sort_sources_legacy(maroons, dist)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:215:    k = min(9, len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:226:        \\\"reachable\\\": len(maroons),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:236:    Pull reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:240:    - The board is an 11x11 orange floor with optional magenta walls and scattered maroon tokens.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:244:    - First flood-fill outward from floor cells touching the target block, moving only through floor or maroon cells,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:245:      and keep only maroon tokens that are reachable through that passable region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:246:    - Sort the reachable maroon tokens by Euclidean distance to the red center, nearest first\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:252:    - Walls still matter, because they decide which maroon tokens are even eligible, but once eligibility is fixed,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/0/code.py:15:#      wires are still 8/5 networks, and maroon 9-regions are still embedded rectangles.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/0/code.py:16:#    - The new observable effect is on the transmitted far-end token only. A maroon rectangle\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/0/code.py:47:#    - The rule is visible without using hidden ids: channels that cross a maroon rectangle produce\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/0/code.py:48:#      the same rest-shape on both ends; channels that avoid maroon keep the original complementary\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/0/code.py:265:    Transmit colored tokens through wire networks while maroon rectangles invert the outbound motif.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/0/code.py:278:      the parity of encountered maroon rectangles controls whether the transmitted complement flips.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:29:      - colors stay orange floor(7), magenta frame/wall(6), green destination ring(3), red center(2), maroon tokens(9)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:30:      - movement is still based on 4-connected flood-fill through floor/maroon cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:31:      - each destination block still fills in row-major order with the closest assigned maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:34:      - maroons are assigned many:many: each token is claimed by the nearest reachable container\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:49:      - each container gets at least one selected maroon from a region that is strictly nearer to that container\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:50:      - at least one selected maroon comes from an overlap region reachable from both containers\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:51:      - optional distractor maroons may appear inside the detached frame, unreachable from both containers\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:57:      - globally rank reachable maroons and pour them into one container\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:61:      - for each maroon, compare both distance maps and assign the token to the nearer block\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:62:      - each block independently sorts its own assigned maroons and fills its own cells in row-major order\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:64:      - with centers at (1,1) and (9,9), a maroon near the upper-left corridor belongs only to the first block\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:65:      - a maroon near the lower-right corridor belongs only to the second block\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:66:      - a maroon near the middle lanes around the detached frame can be reached from both, so ownership must be decided before filling\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:84:    - original global `maroons[:k]` selection is invalid because each container has its own quota and ownership list\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:91:      - source maroons are sampled only from floor cells outside blocks and outside the frame boundary\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:99:      - every accepted sample has maroons owned by both containers\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:100:      - every accepted sample includes at least one overlap maroon reachable from both containers\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:108:    - forcing one private maroon per container plus one contested maroon keeps the rule readable from a few examples\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:223:    overlap_maroons = 0\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:224:    strict_owner_maroons = [0 for _ in containers]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:233:            overlap_maroons += 1\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:238:                strict_owner_maroons[owner] += 1\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:249:        \\\"overlap_maroons\\\": overlap_maroons,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:250:        \\\"strict0\\\": strict_owner_maroons[0] if strict_owner_maroons else 0,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:251:        \\\"strict1\\\": strict_owner_maroons[1] if len(strict_owner_maroons) > 1 else 0,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:258:    Pull maroon pixels into two separated 3x3 containers, each centered on a red marker.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:261:    - The background is orange floor with scattered maroon source pixels and a detached magenta frame in the middle.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:265:    - For each destination block, run a flood-fill distance search through floor/maroon cells, with magenta cells acting as blockers.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:266:    - Each reachable maroon is assigned to the nearest block; equal distances are broken by the row-major order of the red centers.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:267:    - Within each block, its assigned maroons are sorted by distance then row-major position, erased from their source cells, and written into that block in row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:271:    - You must combine two BFS maps with an ownership step: first decide which block owns each maroon, then fill the two containers independently.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:290:    owned_maroons = [[] for _ in containers]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:296:        owned_maroons[owner].append((int(dists[owner][r, c]), r, c))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:299:        owned_maroons[idx].sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:300:        chosen = owned_maroons[idx][: len(dest_cells)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:446:    if features[\\\"overlap_maroons\\\"] < 1:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/1/code.py:14:#    wire endpoints, teal/grey wires route colors across the grid, and maroon rectangles remain\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/1/code.py:15:#    embedded inside those wires. The change is only the role of the maroon rectangle.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/1/code.py:24:#    If its route contains a 2x3 maroon rectangle (area 6), the bottom endpoint still receives\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/1/code.py:25:#    an X. If the route instead contains a 3x3 maroon rectangle (area 9), the bottom endpoint\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/1/code.py:48:#    inspect maroon rectangles and compare examples where a 2x2 / 2x3 rectangle still lets the far\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/1/code.py:253:    Route endpoint tokens across the wire network while maroon rectangles act as parity gates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/1/code.py:268:    - The maroon rectangle is no longer just a connector. Its width-by-height parity is the gate,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:20:# - D13/0 is enforced by generation: the number of reachable maroon sources is exactly k, so the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:28:#   distractor maroons remain to preserve the original flood-fill reachability cue.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:55:def _reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dest_cells: list[tuple[int, int]], dest_set: set[tuple[int, int]], floor: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:82:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9) if int(dist[r, c]) < inf]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:83:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:84:    return maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:93:    Move every reachable maroon source into the row-major prefix of a marked 3x3 block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:96:    - bg = orange floor, optional magenta walls, scattered maroon (9) pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:101:    - Flood-fill from cells adjacent to the destination through floor/maroon cells to find reachable\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:102:      maroon sources.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:105:    - Erase the collected source maroons back to floor. On valid instances, the reachable maroon count\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:108:    Key insight: The red pixel no longer just locates the block; it encodes how many reachable maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:109:    should be collected. Walls still matter because only flood-fill-reachable maroons participate.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:117:    reachable = _reachable_maroons(grid, dest_cells, dest_set, floor)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/20/code.py:22:    if two L-shaped holes appear inside the same frame, one ringed by color 2\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:18:#    - Change 1 (D5/1): source tokens can use several visible colors instead of only maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:21:#      blue -> yellow -> teal -> maroon, and within each color group they are sorted by\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:25:#      [(d=0, blue), (d=1, maroon), (d=2, yellow), (d=3, blue)].\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:26:#      Original task / D5-only variant would place colors [blue, maroon, yellow, blue].\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:27:#      This combo places [blue, blue, yellow, maroon] because both blue tokens must be\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:28:#      consumed before any yellow, and yellow before maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:30:#    - Restrict token colors to a compact palette {blue=1, yellow=4, teal=8, maroon=9}.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:40:#    - `maroons.sort()` was enough before. Now the key must be\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:196:    - Collect every reachable token, sort them first by the fixed visible color-group order blue -> yellow -> teal -> maroon, then within each color by flood-fill distance and row/column, and place the chosen colors into the destination in row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:17:#   Original task: reachable maroon pixels were moved into the 3x3 target block, so the chosen\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:18:#   source cells turned back into orange floor; unreachable maroons stayed where they were.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:19:#   This combo changes both ends at once: chosen reachable maroons are copied into the target\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:20:#   block but remain maroon at their original positions, while unreachable maroons are erased.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:21:#   Example sketch: if two reachable maroons and one walled-off maroon are present, the original\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:22:#   output would keep only two maroons inside the block plus the unreachable distractor; the new\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:23:#   output keeps the two reachable maroons in place, adds two maroons inside the block, and removes\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:27:#   maroons stay in place and the destination uses a single color. To avoid hidden/unobservable\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:28:#   degrees of freedom, the generator only creates 2..9 reachable maroons, so every reachable\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:29:#   maroon is copied and none are silently excluded by the ranking step. It also forces at least\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:33:#   walls=6, floor=7, maroons=9. It also assumes one red center, a 3x3 target around it, at least\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:34:#   one passable opening adjacent to the block, and maroons placed only on floor cells outside the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:37:#   Walls are painted only outside the destination block; maroons are sampled only from floor cells,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:40:#   copies, reachable corridors keep their maroons, and blocked regions become clean floor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:42:#   Across a few examples, a solver can see a stable contrast: maroons connected to a corridor\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:43:#   opening appear twice in the output, while maroons behind walls disappear. No hidden color-value\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:98:def _reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[list[tuple[int, int, int]], np.ndarray]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:126:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:127:    reachable = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < inf]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:134:    Copy reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center, while erasing blocked ones.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:137:    - Orange floor carries scattered maroon pixels, and magenta walls may carve the floor into connected and sealed-off regions.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:141:    - Flood-fill outward from floor or maroon cells touching the destination block, traversing only orange floor and maroon cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:143:    - Those reachable sources stay maroon in place, but any maroon pixel not reached by the flood-fill is erased to orange floor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:146:    - The output separates maroons by connectivity, not by raw proximity: corridor-connected maroons survive and also appear inside the block, while wall-isolated maroons disappear.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:158:    reachable, _dist = _reachable_maroons(grid)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:160:    all_maroons = {(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:161:    unreachable = all_maroons - reachable_set\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/0/code.py:18:#    - 删除原题输入里的青色管道和灰色 crossing 标记；中部改成若干条横向 maroon(9) 墙带，每条墙带只留一个小缺口。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D14/2/code.py:11:#    Variant: the seed is an L-shaped yellow border component in one corner, e.g.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:8:#    - 原题会把 `floor+maroon` 都当作 BFS 通道，所以一条走廊里的整串栗色会一次性全部变成候选，再按距离从近到远选前 k 个。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:18:#    - 原先把 maroon 自己的 BFS 距离直接读出 `dist[r,c]` 不再成立，因为 maroon 不在 BFS 图里；现在距离改为“相邻已达地板的最短距离 + 1”，并额外兼容直接贴住目标块的栗色。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:34:#    - main() 依赖“被收集的栗色底下应当是 floor”；generator 通过先雕 floor 再覆盖 maroon 来保证这一点。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:138:def _reachable_frontier_maroons(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:168:    maroons = [(d, r, c) for (r, c), d in best.items()]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:169:    maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:170:    return maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:182:    initial_frontier = _reachable_frontier_maroons(work, dest_cells, dest_set, floor)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:185:        frontier = _reachable_frontier_maroons(work, dest_cells, dest_set, floor)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:229:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:230:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:231:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:233:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:234:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:244:    Iteratively move the farthest currently exposed maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the lone red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:247:    - Orange cells are the only traversable background; green/red destination cells, magenta walls, and maroon source pixels all behave as solid obstacles.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:248:    - A unique red cell marks the middle of a green 3x3 destination block, while maroon pixels sit on narrow floor corridors or in isolated pockets outside it.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:252:    - At each step, any maroon touching the reached floor region is collectible; choose the farthest such maroon (ties: row, then column), erase it back to floor, and recompute reachability.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:253:    - Stop when the 3x3 block has taken 9 maroons or when no maroon is currently reachable, then write the collected maroons into the destination in row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:256:    - Because maroon pixels now block the flood-fill instead of extending it, a removed maroon can reveal new maroons behind it; the final survivors therefore depend on both the iterative unlocking process and the reversed distance preference.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/22/code.py:55:  - Region pieces span their whole partition bbox via sparse L-shaped pieces,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/1/code.py:260:    - The background is the most common color. Non-background cells form cyan pipe networks, optional maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/6/code.py:10:- 原题的控制源是边缘单像素；这里改成 3 像素、4 连通、单色的 L 形箭头。箭头朝向即发射方向：\\n/home/