o the 3x3 destination by BFS distance.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:19:#    but do not reach the outside ring where most source maroons live.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:35:#    Humans can compare 2-4 examples and spot the rule because the only moving parts are maroon tokens and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:47:#    - At least one full tunnel reaches the exterior, so reachable maroons can always be placed outside.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:48:#    - Distractor pockets are sealed by construction, so unreachable maroons remain unreachable even after\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:120:def _sorted_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dist: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:121:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:122:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < 10**9]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:123:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:124:    return maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:129:    Pull the reachable maroon tokens through the true frame openings into the 3x3 target block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:138:    - Start a flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination block and move through orange or maroon cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:139:    - Only maroon tokens in the same 4-connected component as a real doorway sequence are candidates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:140:    - Sort reachable maroons by BFS distance, then by row and column.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py