/code.py:32:#      an L-shaped hole is filled red by plurality.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D11/0/code.py:33:#      variant: one L-shaped green sprite outside -> the L-shaped hole is filled\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D3/3/code.py:17:#   from red near the source, through grey then maroon, back to red near the arrival end.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/4/code.py:30:    - Example holes after sorting: [area 4 L-shape at left, area 4 bar at right,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/4/code.py:33:      scattered so the bar appears earlier in the input ordering than the L-shape.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:11:#     source_selection: unchanged flood-fill reachability through floor/maroon via 4-neighbors\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:17:#       old: the red center could be overwritten if enough maroons were moved\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:34:#       moved: only the closest 8 maroons enter the outer ring\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:35:#       preserved: the red center stays red and 2 farther reachable maroons remain outside\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:37:#       the partial frontier bends around the perimeter, and saturated cases show a full maroon ring with a red hole\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:43:#       - 4..7 reachable maroons so the spiral prefix is visible\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:44:#       - 9..11 reachable maroons so skipping the center differs from the pure spiral variant that would fill it\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:53:#       - output construction must preserve color 2 at (cr,cc) even when more than 8 reachable maroons exist\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:56:#       - dense-mode examples have at least 9 reachable maroons so the center-skip behavior is exercised\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:58:#     - source maroons are placed only on reachable floor cells, never in the destination or on walls\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:59:#     - extra reachable maroons in dense mode are chosen outside the first 8 ranked cells, so the solver deterministically leaves them behind\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:60:#     - distractor maroons are placed only on unreachable floor cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:169:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center, tracing a spiral that leaves the center untouched.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:172:    - Orange floor cells contain scattered maroon tokens, while magenta walls may block some corridors near the target.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:176:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination through floor/maroon cells; only reachable maroons are movable candidates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:181:    - Two constraints interact: connectivity still decides which maroons qualify, but the destination now behaves like a spiral track wrapped around a permanent red hole.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:200:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:201:    maroons = [triple for triple in maroons if triple[0] < inf]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:202:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:204:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:205:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D12/0/code.py:16:#   grey crossing markers (5), optional maroon pass-through rectangles (9), and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:125:def _bfs_ranked_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, cr: int, cc: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:152:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON) if dist[r, c] >= 0]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:153:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:154:    return maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:163:    ranked = _bfs_ranked_maroons(out, cr, cc)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:240:    Pull the closest straight-line visible maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:248:    - A ray crosses only orange floor and stops at its first non-floor cell; that cell is a candidate only if it is maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:252:    - Being in the same room is no longer enough. The magenta frame puts the block in a corner-biased viewing position, so many maroon pixels are flood-fill reachable but still ignored because no straight ray sees them first.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:386:    total_maroons = int((inp == MAROON).sum())\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:387:    if total_maroons < TOTAL_MAROON_RANGE[0] or total_maroons > TOTAL_MAROON_RANGE[1]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:396:    bfs_ranked = _bfs_ranked_maroons(inp, cr, cc)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:397:    bfs_only_maroons = {(r, c) for _, r, c in bfs_ranked} - visible_cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:398:    if not bfs_only_maroons:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:31:#   - One maroon trigger sits in the first annulus and one in the second annulus. Collecting the first trigger\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:33:#     segment from the outer frame. Additional maroons wait outside the outer frame and are only collectible\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:36:#   - Original task: run one static BFS, keep all reachable maroons, sort once, then fill the destination.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:42:#       5. Re-run BFS again. The outer-border maroons are now reachable and are collected layer by layer.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:44:#       * more maroons move into the 3x3 block;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:52:#   - The first two annuli each contain exactly one trigger maroon. This prevents the dynamic process from\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:59:#       * compute reachable maroons,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:66:#       * total collectible maroons never exceeds the 9 destination cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:72:#   - Unreachable distractors are placed in the opposite sealed corridors. They stay visibly maroon in the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:79:#       * later collected maroons line up beyond the newly opened gates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:398:    Pull maroon pixels into the 3x3 block, but only after they unlock nested wall gates layer by layer.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:406:    - Run BFS from passable cells adjacent to the destination through floor and maroon cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:407:    - Collect only the nearest BFS layer of reachable maroons at a time. After the first-annulus layer is collected, a short middle-frame gate disappears; after the second-annulus layer is collected, a short outer-frame gate disappears.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:408:    - Recompute BFS after each wall change, continue layer by layer, erase every moved source to floor, and fill the destination cells in row-major order with the collected maroons.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:410:    Key insight: Reachability is no longer static. The nested frames define a staged escape path, and the visible wall removals prove that later maroons are not initially reachable; they become collectible only because earlier BFS layers crack open the next shell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:422:    maroons = [\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:427:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:428:    chosen = maroons[: len(DEST_CELLS)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/34/code.py:21:      L-shaped slots inside the frame and one green 1-cell slot elsewhere.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:29:#      orange floor, optional magenta walls, and scattered maroon source pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:30:#    - Reachability is unchanged: only maroons connected to the destination through floor/maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:36:#      smaller flood-fill distance, and if a row still contains several maroons at the same\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:38:#    - Example trace for reachable maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:46:#    - If reachable maroons are <= 9, all of them move and ranking becomes invisible. The\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:47:#      generator therefore uses 10-14 reachable sources so some maroons remain behind.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:55:#      non-maroon non-destination ring cell. The generator reserves one adjacent floor cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:56:#    - BFS through {floor, maroon} still defines eligibility. What changes is only ranking.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:57:#    - The original `maroons.sort()` encoded (distance,row,col). In the combo, ranking must become\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:60:#    - Source maroons are sampled only from reachable floor cells outside the destination block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:68:#    - With >9 reachable maroons, the output exposes the rule through which maroons remain behind.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:69:#      In particular, some earlier-in-column maroons on the same row stay put because a nearer\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:70:#      maroon later in that row is selected first.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:75:#      maroons move versus remain.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:78:#      rows containing multiple reachable maroons require a second observation: closer-in-corridor\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:79:#      maroons win within that row, and equal-distance ties within the row read left-to-right.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:94:#    - `_rank_key(..., \\\"fused\\\")` assumes distance values are defined for every candidate maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:209:    maroons = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:213:            maroons.append((int(r), int(c), d))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:214:    maroons.sort(key=lambda t: _rank_key(t[0], t[1], t[2], mode))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:216:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:217:    chosen = {(r, c) for r, c, _d in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:228:    Move reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 destination around the red center, using a row-first fused ranking.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:231:    - The grid is always 11x11 with a fixed green 3x3 target around one red center, orange floor, optional magenta walls, and maroon pixels scattered on floor cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:232:    - Some maroons are flood-fill reachable from the target through floor/maroon corridors; others may be sealed off behind walls as distractors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:235:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells adjacent to the target, traversing only floor or maroon cells, and keep only reachable maroons as candidates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:237:    - Move up to nine ranked maroons into the destination in destination row-major order, and clear their source cells back to floor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:23:#    - Original rule: a reachable maroon near one corridor gap is moved into the 3x3 target and its old\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:24:#      cell turns back into orange; an unreachable maroon behind a wall stays maroon; the whole 11x11 grid\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:26:#    - Fused rule: that same reachable maroon still moves into the target, but its source cell becomes\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:27:#      gray(5) to mark \\\"collected\\\". A blocked maroon in a sealed corner becomes blue(1) to mark \\\"rejected\\\".\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:31:#      maroon inside the target = packed token, gray = consumed reachable source, blue = unreachable source.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:35:#      maroon tokens, gray traces, blue rejects.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:48:#    - Gray traces are only meaningful for moved sources, so generator places exactly k reachable maroons:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:53:#      coordinate sets. Corner pockets are isolated by added wall cells before maroons are placed.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:57:#      rejects, and maroon packed tokens, but the layout is still structured: blue is forced into sealed\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:58:#      crop corners, gray is forced onto reachable crop cells, and maroon fill stays inside the 3x3 target.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:182:    Pack reachable maroon tokens into the central 3x3 target, leave gray pickup traces, repaint blocked maroons blue, then crop to the target neighborhood.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:186:    - Magenta wall segments create corridor gaps and sealed pockets around that target, while maroon tokens sit on floor cells outside the 3x3 block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:189:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the target through orange/maroon cells, then rank reachable maroons by BFS distance with row-major tie-breaks.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:190:    - Move the closest reachable maroons into the 3x3 target in row-major order, turn each consumed source gray, and recolor every unreachable maroon blue.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:194:    - The crop hides the distant corridors, so the important evidence is local: maroon inside the 3x3 block means \\\"selected\\\", gray means \\\"reachable and consumed\\\", and blue means \\\"blocked out by walls\\\".\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:48:#      a 3-cell L-shaped corner bite produces a 2-lane diagonal band.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D4/3/code.py:261:    Send split 3x3 tokens through the wire permutation, using an asymmetric pair of complementary L-shapes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:19:#      maroon cells, and anything beyond the 3x3 capacity simply stays outside.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:24:#      If reachable maroons exceed that capacity, the spill does not stay put:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:25:#      the extra reachable maroons continue into the one-cell-thick outer ring\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:29:#      If 13 reachable maroons exist, output fills the first 13 square cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:30:#      If 19 reachable maroons exist, output fills all 16 square cells and then\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:33:#      extra maroons would remain at their source locations.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:47:#    - \\\"overflow maroons are untouched\\\" is invalid.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:56:#      never collide with walls and source/distractor maroons never start inside\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:61:#    - Overflow is directly visible because the maroon fill expands from the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:62:#      square into a second surrounding layer, not just \\\"some maroons remain\\\".\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:76:#      the square is full, the same maroon payload continues into the ring.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:211:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into a variable-size square, then spill overflow into its surrounding ring.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:214:    - Orange floor contains optional magenta walls and scattered maroon (9) pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:218:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells touching the square, traversing only floor and maroon cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:219:    - Sort reachable maroon pixels by BFS distance, then by row and column.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:220:    - Fill the square in row-major order first; if reachable maroons still remain, continue filling the one-cell-thick outer ring around that square in row-major order. Moved maroons are erased back to floor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:240:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:241:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < INF]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:242:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:244:    moved = maroons[: min(len(targets), len(maroons))]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/48/code.py:27:    - Example: suppose the frame contains five identical L-shaped holes arranged as\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:11:#     connectivity: candidate maroons are still determined only by 4-connected flood-fill through floor/maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:14:#       old: sort reachable maroons by (bfs_distance, row, col)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:19:#       old: write the chosen maroons into the 3x3 block in row-major order\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:32:#       setup: 6 reachable maroons, all of them move\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:37:#       setup: 10 reachable maroons on the same bfs shell around the destination\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:38:#       original: 9 chosen maroons are the row-major earliest shell cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:39:#       combo: 9 chosen maroons are the clockwise-earliest shell cells from the top\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:40:#       visible_difference: the leftover outside maroon moves to a different side of the ring, even though the destination ends up full\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:56:#       - walls remain hard blockers because bfs only walks on floor/maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:60:#       - generator can no longer assume \\\"exactly k reachable maroons\\\" is enough to expose every change\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:63:#       - angle-visible boards must guarantee a same-distance shell with at least 10 maroons and different row-vs-angle top-9 subsets\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:66:#     - source maroons are placed only on reachable floor cells, never inside the destination or on walls\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:67:#     - distractor maroons are placed only on unreachable floor cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:171:def _rank_reachable_maroons(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:178:    maroons = [\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:183:    maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (t[0], t[1], t[2], t[3]))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:184:    return maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:187:def _row_rank_reachable_maroons(dist: np.ndarray, maroons: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:188:    return sorted((int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in maroons)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:203:    reachable_maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere((grid == 9) & (dist < 10**9))]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:204:    moved = min(len(fill_order), len(reachable_maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:205:    angle_ranked = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, dist, cr, cc)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:206:    row_ranked = _row_rank_reachable_maroons(dist, reachable_maroons)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:213:    angle_active = 1 if len(reachable_maroons) > len(fill_order) and angle_chosen != row_chosen else 0\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:216:        \\\"reachable\\\": len(reachable_maroons),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:224:    Move reachable maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center using clockwise tie-breaks and a spiral fill.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:227:    - Orange floor cells form the passable background, magenta walls may block parts of it, and maroon tokens sit on some floor cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:231:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination, treating floor and maroon as traversable; only reachable maroons are eligible.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:232:    - Sort eligible maroons by BFS distance, then break same-distance ties by clockwise angle around the red center starting from straight up.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:233:    - Move the first nine-or-fewer maroons: erase their source cells back to floor and write them into the destination along a fixed clockwise outer-to-inner spiral.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:236:    - The same center controls both decisions: outside the block it orders tied maroons by rotation, and inside the block it lays the moved maroons down in the matching clockwise spiral.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:252:    maroons = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, dist, cr, cc)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:253:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:254:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:480:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9) if int(dist[r, c]) < 10**9]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:481:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:482:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:483:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D9/1/code.py:196:    Eject content pixels from L-shaped cup frames outward along each cup's spike direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:22:#   wall opening. In a concrete example, a maroon one step outside the right\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:27:#   eight edge cells of the 3x3 block. The same right-side maroon can be ranked\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:28:#   before a farther-left maroon even if its actual corridor path is longer.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:29:# - This only affects the output when there are more than 9 reachable maroons;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:30:#   otherwise every reachable maroon moves. The generator therefore guarantees\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:31:#   at least 10 reachable maroons and rejects layouts where the new top-9 set is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:42:#   maroons after the 3x3 block is filled, and those leftovers differ from the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:43:#   old BFS-based choice. The user can compare \\\"which reachable maroons stayed\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:123:def _reachable_maroons_sorted(grid: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:126:    maroons = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:130:            maroons.append((_edge_distance(rr, cc, edge_cells), rr, cc))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:131:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:132:    return maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:163:    Move the nine edge-nearest reachable maroon pixels into the centered 3x3 block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:166:    - The board is 11x11 with orange floor, optional magenta wall barriers, scattered maroon pixels,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:173:      and maroon cells but never through magenta walls.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:174:    - Among the maroon pixels reached by that flood-fill, rank them by the minimum Manhattan distance\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:176:    - Move the first nine ranked maroons (or all of them if fewer exist) into the destination block\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:181:    corridor length. A maroon that is geometrically close to one side of the block can outrank another\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:182:    maroon whose actual path from the center is shorter.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:194:    maroons = _reachable_maroons_sorted(grid)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:195:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:196:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:330:    new_rank = {(r, c) for _, r, c in _reachable_maroons_sorted(probe)[:9]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:382:    reachable_maroons = _reachable_maroons_sorted(inp)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:383:    if len(reachable_maroons) <= 9:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:397:    new_top9 = {(r, c) for _, r, c in reachable_maroons[:9]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:18:#       optional maroon 9-rect pass-through blocks inside the cyan/grey wire.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:401:      optional maroon pass-through rectangles, and 3x3 tokens near wire endpoints.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/0/code.py:15:#     solids: 2 basin colors still build bottom-anchored walls / L-shapes / short stair blocks\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:14:#    - Original task ranked reachable maroons the same way as before, but then wrote them into all 9\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:20:#    - Example with k=6 reachable maroons:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:35:#    - Generator never places walls or maroons inside the 3x3 destination block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:87:def _reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dest_cells: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:116:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:117:    maroons = [triple for triple in maroons if triple[0] < inf]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:118:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:119:    return maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:124:    Move the nearest reachable maroon pixels into the green frame around the unique red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:127:    - The board uses orange floor, optional magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and one red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:131:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the 3x3 destination block, traveling through orange or maroon cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:132:    - Rank reachable maroon tokens by BFS distance, then by row and column.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:152:    reachable = _reachable_maroons(grid, dest_cells)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:17:     L-shaped arrow is attached near the tail side. The arrow is 8-connected to\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:10:#       - reachable maroons are selected by BFS distance from the central 3x3 block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:11:#       - maroons cut off by magenta walls are ignored and remain where they are.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:13:#       - D18/2 changes those blocked maroons into active movers that travel along the wall network.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:18:#     - Put blocked maroons in 1-cell side pockets between the two rings; each pocket touches the wall graph through two short connectors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:22:#       - a top-pocket maroon cannot be reached from the center because the top inner wall cell is closed.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:25:#       - the same top-pocket maroon first attaches to adjacent magenta wall cells,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:27:#       - if that mouth is an inner opening on another side, the maroon becomes reachable and may join the central fill,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:30:#       - the new wall mouths are not cosmetic: they change both the nearest target of blocked maroons and the final ranking pool for the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:34:#     - The generator always includes both outcomes: one blocked maroon that reaches an inner opening and one that stops at an outer opening.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:37:#       - unreachable maroons can no longer be ignored before ranking.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:38:#       - clearing only originally reachable sources is no longer sufficient because blocked maroons relocate first.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:40:#       - blocked maroons must touch the wall graph; the generator guarantees this with side pockets.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:42:#       - two blocked maroons should not compete for one target opening; the generator probes the layout and rejects collisions.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:43:#       - pocket sides cannot have an inner opening on the same side, otherwise the pocket maroon would already be reachable.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:46:#     - Reachable source maroons are sampled only from floor cells that are not pockets and not any potential opening cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:48:#     - The wall network is a clean square-with-frame motif, so widened mouths and moved maroons stand out immediately.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:302:def _move_blocked_maroons(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:315:    maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:316:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:317:    for r, c in maroons:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:406:    staged, moved = _move_blocked_maroons(np.asarray(grid, dtype=int), CENTER_R, CENTER_C, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:408:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(staged == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:409:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:410:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:411:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[: min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:427:    Route blocked maroon pixels to the nearest wall mouth, then fill the center block with the closest reachable maroons.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:431:    - Magenta walls form an inner ring and an outer frame, with visible side openings of width 1 or 2 and a few maroon pixels trapped in side pockets.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:434:    - First, flood-fill reachability from the destination through floor and maroon cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:435:    - Any maroon that is still blocked travels along adjacent magenta wall cells to the nearest open wall mouth; inner mouths make it newly reachable, outer mouths only relocate it.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:436:    - After those relocations, recompute reachability, rank reachable maroons by distance then row-major tie-break, and move the closest ones into the 3x3 destination in row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:439:    - The wall openings matter twice: they are both pass-through corridors for the center flood-fill and the landing targets for previously unreachable maroons, so extra or wider mouths can change which maroons ultimately enter the block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:451:    staged, _ = _move_blocked_maroons(grid, cr, cc, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:454:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(staged == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:455:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:456:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:458:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:459:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:497:    staged_probe, moved_probe = _move_blocked_maroons(probe, CENTER_R, CENTER_C, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:42:#    - Walls are written only outside dest_set. Source and distractor maroons are\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:49:#      still teaches \\\"reachable maroons only\\\" before the write-path twist.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:170:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the irregular destination shape using a spiral-with-skips fill.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:173:    - Orange floor cells may be split by magenta walls, and maroon tokens sit on some floor cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:177:    - Recover the full red+green container, then flood-fill outward through floor/maroon cells touching it to find reachable maroon candidates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:178:    - Rank reachable maroons by BFS distance, then by row and column, erase the closest ones from their source cells, and place them into the container.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:182:    - Two geometric inferences interact: walls still decide which maroons are eligible, but the destination is an irregular shape whose fill order is defined by a spiral on its enclosing rectangle rather than by row-major order on the shape itself.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:222:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:223:    maroons = [triple for triple in maroons if triple[0] < inf]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:224:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:226:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:227:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:25:#    - Example: if a blue chain goes upward from the target, a maroon sitting in a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:28:#      blue. A maroon beyond the tip of the chain is reachable, because the motion\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:57:#    - The generator always places distractor maroons inside blue-side pockets.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:197:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:198:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < 10**9]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:199:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:201:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:202:    chosen = [(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:246:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:247:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:248:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:249:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:250:    chosen = [(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:261:    Move the nearest legally reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:264:    - Orange floor carries scattered maroon tokens, while the target is the usual 3x3 green block with one red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:269:    - Sideways turns out of a blue cell are illegal, so maroons in side pockets touching a blue ray are not reachable; reachable maroons are ranked by directed distance and then fill the target in row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:23:#      Inside that square, placement is no longer row-major. The moved maroons follow\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:26:#      If reachable maroons exceed the square capacity, the next maroons do not stay\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:31:#      old task with 12 reachable maroons:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:33:#      this combo with a 4x4 square and 19 reachable maroons:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:35:#        surrounding spill ring, and only the still-later maroons would remain outside.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:36:#      this combo with a 5x5 square and 11 reachable maroons:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:60:#    - \\\"overflow maroons just stay put\\\" is invalid. The solver must erase not only the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:61:#      maroons moved inside the square, but also the extra selected maroons moved onto\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:66:#      non-destination, non-maroon color in the whole grid.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:76:#    - Source maroons and distractors are sampled only from floor cells, never from\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:92:#    - The generator also keeps source maroons off the spill ring in the input, so the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:97:#      floor, wall, green square, red anchor, maroon tokens.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:102:#    - Non-overflow samples are forced to be partial fills (at least 6 maroons and at\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:105:#      extra maroons is capped to a small visible band so the spill ring activates\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:280:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into a variable-size square, and spill any excess onto the square's outer ring.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:283:    - Orange floor cells may be partitioned by magenta walls, with maroon tokens scattered on reachable and unreachable floor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:287:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the square, traversing only floor and maroon cells, then rank reachable maroons by BFS distance, row, and column.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:288:    - Fill the square first along a clockwise inward spiral. If more ranked maroons remain after the square is full, continue by placing them on the one-cell-thick ring immediately outside the square in clockwise perimeter order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:289:    - Every moved maroon is erased from its source cell back to floor; unreachable maroons and any maroons beyond the supported spill ring remain in place.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:292:    - The solver must recover both the square size and the two-stage write geometry. The square size sets the internal capacity, while overflow activates a second visible path just outside the square instead of leaving extra reachable maroons on the floor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:305:    reachable_maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:306:    reachable_maroons = [item for item in reachable_maroons if item[0] < 10**9]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:307:    reachable_maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:309:    inner_count = min(len(fill_path), len(reachable_maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:310:    overflow_count = min(len(spill_order), max(0, len(reachable_maroons) - inner_count))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:312:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in reachable_maroons[:moved_total]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:153:def _old_bfs_ranked_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dest_set: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:298:    Move the closest maroon pixels that are directly visible through the frame openings into the central 3×3 block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:302:    - The frame is mostly solid, but some non-corner side cells are single-cell openings; maroon pixels are scattered outside the frame.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:306:    - That first blocking cell contributes only if it is maroon, so a frame opening exposes at most one candidate on that line while a wall cell blocks the ray immediately.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:310:    - The puzzle is about line of sight through explicit rectangular-frame openings, not about general corridor connectivity. A maroon pixel may still be reachable after exiting an opening, but if it requires a turn or sits behind another blocker on the same ray, it stays where it is.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:388:    ranked_old = _old_bfs_ranked_maroons(base, dest_set)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D14/1/code.py:63:#       - the pipe network is entirely cyan/8, with no grey or maroon helper colors\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:15:#    are directly adjacent to that block. Reachable maroon cells are found by BFS from the block's\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:19:#      input full grid contains a 7x7 framed region plus extra outside maroons;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:22:#      after moving the closest reachable maroons into the block, the result is cropped to the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:33:#    - Unreachable maroons can survive in the full grid but vanish from the final answer purely\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:44:#    hidden. Reachable maroons are visibly the ones inside the frame; outside maroons disappear\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:47:#    The three layers do not overlap: the block uses green/red, the channel uses orange/maroon, and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:153:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the central 3x3 block, then crop to the enclosing frame.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:156:    - The canvas contains orange floor, scattered maroon tokens, a unique red center inside a 3x3 green block,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:158:    - The frame is not adjacent to the block: a 1-2 cell orange channel separates them, and maroons may appear\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:162:    - Flood-fill from passable cells adjacent to the 3x3 block through orange/maroon cells; maroons reached by\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:164:    - Sort reachable maroons by distance to the block, breaking ties by row then column, and place the closest\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:169:    Key insight: The magenta border now defines both connectivity and the crop boundary; only maroons inside the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:268:    # Independent expectation: only maroons in the inner channel are reachable because the frame is closed.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/9/code.py:25:#    - Replace the single maroon source class with multicolor single-pixel sources. This combo\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/9/code.py:39:#      dist 0-1 -> maroon(9), dist 2-3 -> gray(5), dist 4+ -> yellow(4).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/9/code.py:47:#    - The original floor-color inference relied on maroon being the only non-structural color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:19:      - floor/wall/maroon color roles stay the same\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:21:      - reachability still uses 4-connected BFS through floor+maroon cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:22:      - each destination still fills in row-major order with its owned maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:25:      - the mapping is many:many: many maroons may feed many blocks, and a block\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:26:        competes with the others for shared maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:44:      distractors: optional unreachable maroons that remain in place\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:49:      - one BFS distance map ranks all reachable maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:50:      - the first k maroons fill that single container\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:54:      - every maroon compares all reachable containers and is owned by the nearest\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:55:      - each container fills only from its owned maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:57:      - suppose a maroon lies in the central corridor and is reachable from the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:81:    - original global `maroons[:k]` slice is invalid because each container has\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:88:      - merely selecting contested maroons is not enough, because the output only\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:92:        input maroons than it actually owns after competition\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:94:        \\\"every container uses every reachable maroon independently\\\" reading\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:100:      - maroons are sampled only from floor cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:106:      - at least two containers receive contested maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:108:        maroons are owned by another container\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:372:    Route reachable maroon pixels into several 3x3 destination blocks around red centers.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:375:    - The board is an 11x11 floor-and-wall maze with scattered maroon (9) pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:379:    - For every destination block, compute BFS reachability through floor/maroon cells, stopping at walls.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:380:    - Each reachable maroon is owned by the nearest destination block; equal distances break by center row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:381:    - Every block sorts only its owned maroons by distance and writes them into its own 3x3 cells in row-major order, erasing the moved sources back to floor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:385:    - Shared corridors create maroons that more than one block can reach, so you must compare several BFS frontiers first and only then refill each block from its assigned pool.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:408:    owned_maroons = [[] for _ in containers]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:414:        owned_maroons[owner].append((int(dists[owner][r, c]), r, c))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:417:        owned_maroons[idx].sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:418:        chosen = owned_maroons[idx][: len(dest_cells)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D13/2/code.py:24:#   L-shapes whose corner is exactly the companion dot.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D13/2/code.py:53:# - Candidate L-shapes are rejected if their output cells overlap another line's\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D13/2/code.py:67:# - Outputs are built from non-overlapping L-shapes only; no dense criss-cross\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D13/2/code.py:149:      of an L-shape, and the same period is replayed on the orthogonal axis from\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:16:#    with a left-hand rule. Maroons on the walked route move inward; maroons in side branches stay put.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:25:# 5. Visual observability: every valid sample includes at least one maroon in a branch that BFS could reach\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:188:    Pull maroon tokens from the left-hand wall-follow route of a maze into the 3x3 block around the red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:198:    - Collect maroons encountered on that traced route, erase them from their source cells, then fill the destination in row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:202:      so branch maroons that flood-fill could reach still remain in place unless the left-hand trace actually passes through them.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:216:    maroons = [(r, c) for r, c in trace_cells if int(grid[r, c]) == MAROON]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:217:    k = min(len(DEST_CELLS), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:219:    for r, c in maroons[:k]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/1/code.py:402:    - Background cells stay empty; non-background cells form 3x3 tokens plus a cyan/grey/maroon pipe network whose junction rows can be read in two ways.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/8/code.py:78:#    - Extra noise is limited to small lines/L-shapes/blocks whose local degree\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/6/code.py:18:#    - The opening direction is still the corner it touches: NW / NE / SE / SW.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/6/code.py:41:#    - Wide bands can form an L-shaped front (size 3), so lockstep grouping must\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/8/code.py:23:      - 一个蓝色 L 形块位于列 6 左侧，且其 bbox 中心离列 6 比离行 9 更近，所以它绕列 6 左右镜像\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:14:#    Example corridor: dest -> orange -> maroon A -> maroon B -> orange -> maroon C.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:15:#    Original dd6b8c4b treats maroon as passable, so A/B/C are all reachable in one BFS.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:23:#    - `passable = {floor, 9}` is no longer valid: maroon must block flood-fill.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:25:#      every collected maroon, so distances must be recomputed iteratively.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:26:#    - \\\"There is a passable start next to the destination\\\" is no longer guaranteed: a maroon can\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:27:#      sit directly at the opening, so the solver must allow direct-adjacent maroon targets even\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:34:#    marks hard obstacles, and maroon chains visibly sit inside the tunnels they block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:40:#    because some moved maroons are not initially exposed; they appear to come from behind others.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:43:#    the original \\\"floor+maroon are both passable\\\" ranking. The generator therefore measures the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:102:def _maroon_candidates(grid: np.ndarray, dest_cells: list[tuple[int, int]], dest_set: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:144:        candidates = _maroon_candidates(work, dest_cells, dest_set)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:157:    return [(r, c) for _dist, r, c in _maroon_candidates(np.asarray(grid, dtype=int), dest_cells, dest_set)[:max_take]]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:161:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Reference helper for the original dd6b8c4b connectivity model: floor+maroon are passable.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:199:    Collect maroon tokens into the 3x3 target one at a time, recomputing reachability after each pick.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:202:    - Orange is the only traversable background; magenta walls and maroon tokens are both solid blockers.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:207:    - At each step, consider maroon tokens touching that flood region (or touching the destination directly),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:11:  and maroon rectangular pass-through blocks (9).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:27:  diamonds, and may include 0-3 maroon pass-through rectangles that widen one\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:36:  maroon blocks are unchanged in meaning.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:37:- `_trace_wire` assumes a wire may enter a maroon rectangle and must leave from\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:199:    Follow one wire until its far endpoint, passing straight through maroon blocks.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:269:    - Background cells surround several vertical cyan wire channels, sometimes widened by maroon rectangles, with 3x3 solid or X tokens sitting two cells beyond channel endpoints.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:395:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Attempt to place one straight pass-through maroon rectangle.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/5/code.py:48:#    - 三个碰撞点在模板中呈 L 形分布, 混色局部之间只有留白或原色线段, 不会糊成一团.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D6/1/code.py:11:#       - a bottom-anchored basin network with a left wall, a low L-shaped divider, and a taller divider;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:24:#   original: 5-pixel plus -> phase tile -> always 16x16 lattice -> centered 6x6 maroon stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:25:#   variant:  5-pixel plus -> phase tile -> 15x15 lattice -> centered 6x6 maroon stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:62:# - The output still has only two layers: a repeated orange/black lattice and a centered maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:69:#   color; output uses only black, orange, and maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:121:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a variable-size periodic lattice whose side length is set by the glyph's pixel count, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:131:    - Fill that canvas by tiling the phase tile, then place a centered 6x6 maroon stamp made from a 2x2 tiling of the original glyph.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:9:#    - solver 仍先从目标块外侧相邻的可通行单元做 flood-fill, 只把能通过 floor/maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:31:#      1. 候选排序从 `maroons.sort()` 改成按 `(-dist,row,col)`。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:45:#    - 通过限制 total maroon 数量与墙样式, 保持版面稀疏, 避免目标块附近过度拥挤。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:47:#    - 没有新增颜色语义。所有变化仍是 maroon 在 floor 与目标块之间移动。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:162:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:163:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:164:    return dest_cells, fill_order, floor, maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:170:    dest_cells, fill_order, floor, maroons = _reachable_analysis(grid)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:173:        maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:175:        maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:178:    k = min(len(write_order), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:179:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:192:    Move the outermost reachable maroon pixels into the central 3x3 block, filling it from bottom-right backward.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:196:    - Magenta walls may carve corridors around that block, and maroon tokens are scattered on floor cells outside it.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:199:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination, moving only through floor or maroon cells, to find reachable maroon candidates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:201:    - Remove the chosen sources and place the moved maroons into the destination in reverse row-major order, starting at the lower-right corner.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:204:    - The same wall-gated reachability test from the original task still decides which maroons are eligible, but both downstream directions are inverted: selection prefers the farthest candidates and writing prefers the bottom-right end of the block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:20:      - Keep the original 2x2 maroon stamp of the 3x3 glyph, so the stamp is still 6x6.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:36:    - Overwriting lattice cells with maroon is still safe because the original task already allowed the stamp to cover the lattice.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:43:    - A left/right or top/bottom shift is immediately visible because the maroon stamp is large and contrasts with the orange/black lattice.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:94:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice and place the maroon 2x2 stamp at a location derived from the glyph's input position.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:104:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2, recolor its True cells to maroon, and treat that as a 6x6 stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:108:    - The glyph's shape still chooses the lattice phase, but the glyph's position in the 6x6 input now also encodes where the maroon stamp belongs on the 16x16 output.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:22:#      pixel, green around it, orange floor, optional magenta wall barriers, and maroon tokens on\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:24:#    - Reachability is unchanged: only maroons connected to the destination through a 4-neighbor\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:25:#      flood-fill over floor+maroon cells are eligible.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:27:#      1) source ranking order = row-major scan over reachable maroons, i.e. sort by (row, col);\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:31:#      reachable maroons = {(1,8),(2,2),(8,1),(9,9),...}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:34:#      then places the moved maroons down the first column of the target before moving right.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:35:#    - Because the task always moves k = min(9, reachable_count) maroons, there is an unavoidable\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:37:#      * if reachable_count > 9, the source ranking is visible because some reachable maroons stay\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:39:#      * if reachable_count < 9, the column-major fill is visible, but every reachable maroon moves,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:55:#    - The original `maroons.sort()` encoded distance ranking directly. That assumption is replaced\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:56:#      with sorting reachable maroons by coordinates only.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:57:#    - Floor-color inference still needs at least one visible non-maroon ring-adjacent cell. The\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:63:#    - Source maroons are sampled only from reachable floor cells outside the destination.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:70:#    - Scan-order source selection is visible through which reachable maroons remain on the floor\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:74:#    - Walls still provide clear corridor structure, so reachable and unreachable maroons remain\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:78:#      among visible maroons and the fill trajectory inside the fixed 3x3 target.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:89:#      and at least one visible non-maroon neighbor color around the target for floor inference.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:152:    assert cand_ring, \\\"ring around destination must contain at least one visible non-maroon color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:229:    Move reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 target around the unique red center, ranking by scan position and filling by columns.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:236:    - Flood-fill from passable cells adjacent to the destination through floor and maroon cells to determine which maroon pixels are reachable.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:237:    - Ignore path distance when ordering those reachable maroons: sort them only by row first, then column, erase the first up to nine source cells, and place those maroons into the destination in column-major order from the top-left.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:238:    - Destination cells beyond the moved count keep their original green/red colors, and unreachable maroons remain unchanged.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:241:    - The problem separates eligibility from placement: walls still decide which maroons can move, but once reachability is known the source order is a global scan order while the destination uses a different, column-first traversal.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/17/code.py:26:#   1. 输入左上角附近有一个红十字：水平轴 r=1、垂直轴 c=1；一个绿色 L 形 seed 只在右下象限。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:16:#   structure is the 6x6 maroon stamp made by tiling the glyph 2x2: instead of\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:21:#   In the source task, a plus glyph always produced the same centered maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:23:#   but its 6x6 maroon overlay starts at (0,0). Likewise an H still decodes to the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:40:#   Overlap with the orange/black lattice is intentional and safe because maroon is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:43:#   The maroon overlay is large and isolated, so moving it from center to a corner\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:118:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a 16x16 periodic lattice with the motif stamped in maroon at a glyph-specific corner.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:128:    - Tile the input glyph 2x2 into a 6x6 maroon stamp, then place that stamp in a corner chosen by glyph type rather than at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:131:    - The input object still serves as a code for two output attributes: its contour determines the lattice phase, and that same contour class now also chooses which corner receives the maroon stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:8:# - Baseline dd6b8c4b: the magenta barrier hugs the 3x3 green/red destination. Reachable maroons are found by\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:9:#   floor BFS from cells immediately outside the block; maroons trapped behind the wall are ignored and stay put.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:14:# - D18/2 change: blocked maroons are not static distractors. Each trapped maroon sits in a sealed 1-cell pocket\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:17:#   recompute which maroons are reachable from the center block and fill the block by distance.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:18:# - Example trace: a maroon in the left-upper pocket at (3,1) is surrounded by wall on all four sides, so the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:20:#   is open, the maroon follows the frame around the top-left corner to the top opening at (0,5). From that new\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:27:# - Pockets are single-cell chambers, so each moved maroon has a unique origin. Openings are one cell wide and are\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:29:# - The generator enforces 2-3 moving maroons, at least one moved maroon that later fills the center block, at\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:30:#   least one moved maroon that remains visible at an opening, and a wall-path length threshold. This prevents the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:36:# - Original assumption: unreachable maroons can be ignored forever. Broken by D18/2. Now they may become reachable\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:38:# - Original assumption: clearing only the chosen reachable source cells is sufficient. Broken because moved maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:41:#   1. Every trapped maroon is adjacent to at least one wall cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:43:#   3. Different trapped maroons are assigned distinct nearest openings.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:51:# - Reachable source maroons are sampled only from orange floor cells that are not pockets and not opening slots.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:55:#   is the D14 part. They can also see maroons disappear from sealed side pockets and reappear on border openings,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:62:#   a handful of isolated pocket/source maroons. No region carries multiple kinds of markup on top of each other.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:63:# - Because pockets are tiny and sparse, the output does not become cluttered even when one moved maroon remains on\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:64:#   the frame while other maroons fill the center block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:68:#   behavior, if at least two blocked maroons actually move along the frame, and if the moved maroons exhibit both\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:187:def _move_blocked_maroons(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:198:    maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:199:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:200:    for r, c in maroons:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:240:def _select_reachable_maroons(\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:245:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:246:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:247:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:248:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:249:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:250:    return maroons, chosen\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:254:    maroons, chosen = _select_reachable_maroons(grid, dest_cells)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:255:    _ = maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:266:    Route trapped maroons along a detached border frame, then use the closest reachable maroons to fill the center block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:271:    - Some maroons are ordinary reachable floor tokens, while others sit inside tiny sealed pockets attached to the frame.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:274:    - First, detect maroons that are unreachable from the center through orange/maroon floor travel.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:275:    - Each such blocked maroon moves along the connected magenta frame to the nearest valid side-center opening.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:276:    - After all blocked maroons relocate, recompute reachability and move the closest reachable maroons into the 3x3 block in row-major order, erasing the selected source positions.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:291:    staged, _ = _move_blocked_maroons(grid, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:292:    _maroons, chosen = _select_reachable_maroons(staged, dest_cells)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:339:    staged, moved = _move_blocked_maroons(np.asarray(grid, dtype=int), dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:340:    _maroons, chosen = _select_reachable_maroons(staged, dest_cells)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:398:    staged_probe, moved_probe = _move_blocked_maroons(probe, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/35/code.py:75:#      insets, or L-shapes. Only a handful of interior anomalies are injected,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/20/code.py:15:#      * 输入: 左上有蓝色 L 形贴着一条竖红线, 更右下还有一条横红线和一个孤立红点, 后两者附近为空。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:16:#      green 3x3 target block and moves through floor/maroon cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:48:#    - At least one blocked mouth exists, and at least four maroons lie in the 8-only reachable set.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:162:    maroons = [\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:167:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:169:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:170:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:181:    Move the nearest 8-reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:192:      maroon pixels as passable and magenta as blocking.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:193:    - Collect only maroon pixels reached by that 8-connected search.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:194:    - Sort reachable maroons by distance, then row, then column, and copy the closest ones into\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:250:    maroon_cells = {(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:251:    only8_maroons = maroon_cells & (reach8 - reach4)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:258:        \\\"only8_maroons\\\": len(only8_maroons),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:260:        \\\"nearest_only8_dist\\\": min((int(dist8[r, c]) for r, c in only8_maroons), default=-1),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:292:    if metrics[\\\"only8_maroons\\\"] < FILL_RANGE[0] or metrics[\\\"output_diff\\\"] <= 0:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:27:      color: recolor foreground to maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:63:    - size 4 and size 5 motifs differ by obvious stroke thickness and by the size of the central maroon stamp\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:67:    - there are only three output colors (black, orange, maroon), as in the original task\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:68:    - the maroon stamp occupies one centered block, while the lattice remains readable around it\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:166:    Decode a 4x4 or 5x5 enlarged contour glyph into a larger-period orange lattice and stamp the glyph family back in maroon at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:176:    - Fill a black 28x28 canvas by repeating that phase tile, then place a 2x2 maroon copy of the original enlarged glyph at the canvas center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/32/code.py:289:    - Black regions may also contain isolated single-pixel noise specks in several other colors (for example red, green, yellow, teal, or maroon) rather than only blue.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:36:#   reachable maroons, so the destination can only accept a subset.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:39:#   maroon back to inferred floor\\\". All three are unsafe now. This solver uses a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:41:#   generator guarantees every maroon sits on an orange endpoint so erasing a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:64:    MAROON: 1,  # generator places maroons on orange corridor endpoints\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:166:def _rank_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, *, weighted: bool) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:186:    ranked = _rank_reachable_maroons(g, weighted=True)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:199:    Move the lowest-cost reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:204:    - Orange and grey corridor cells are both traversable; scattered maroon pixels sit on corridor endpoints.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:207:    - Start from corridor cells adjacent to the destination block and search through orange, grey, and maroon cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:208:    - Entering orange or maroon costs 1, while entering grey costs 2.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:209:    - Rank reachable maroons by total path cost, breaking ties by row then column.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:210:    - Move the best-ranked maroons into the destination in row-major order and erase their source cells back to orange.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:241:    weighted = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, weighted=True)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:242:    plain = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, weighted=False)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:23:#      keeping the maroon phase glyph legible.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:28:#    - Reusing the whole boolean motif as the center stamp would incorrectly recolor decoration cells to maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:37:#    - Both colors are chosen from non-special ARC colors excluding black, orange, and maroon; they are distinct.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:39:#    - Across examples, one input color controls the global orange lattice and the maroon core glyph, while the other\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:47:#    - The maroon phase stamp and the decoration layer are disjoint by construction, avoiding ambiguous overpainting.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:50:#      the phase color is interpreted structurally: its shape becomes the orange lattice code plus a maroon stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:148:    - Tile the canonical glyph 2x2 in maroon at the center, and tile the other color's mask 2x2 as an additional\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88bcf3b4/D9/0/code.py:4:# 现在改为沿 bar 前进方向的正交方向做纯水平/纯垂直延伸；整体从 V 形退出改为 L 形退出。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D15/0/code.py:14:#   The output keeps the 16x16 size and the centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp, but the orange/black carrier\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D15/0/code.py:28:#   The centered maroon overwrite remains safe because it intentionally sits on top of the lattice in both\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D15/0/code.py:38:#   The output still has only two layers: a black/orange background lattice and a maroon central stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D15/0/code.py:42:#   maroon for the center stamp, exactly as in the seed task.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D15/0/code.py:85:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 diagonal lattice with the motif stamped in maroon at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D15/0/code.py:96:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:25:#      with the same phase decode and centered maroon stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:44:#    - Humans can compare the edge bars with the maroon 6x6 center stamp in the output and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:53:#      orange, and maroon only. Colors are role-based and unchanged from the original\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:156:    Read a border legend that encodes a contour glyph, then expand it into the same 16x16 phase lattice and centered maroon stamp as the original task family.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:166:    - Tile the phase over a black 16x16 canvas, then stamp a 2x2 maroon tiling of the reconstructed glyph into the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:169:    - The input foreground no longer marks the glyph directly inside the field; it is a border template that must be read first, and only the reconstructed motif controls both the lattice phase and the central maroon stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:23:#    - D13/2 then changes what happens when too few reachable maroons exist:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:24:#      the solver still ranks reachable maroons by BFS distance, but if fewer\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:28:#      input square = 5x5, reachable maroons = 6.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:29:#      Old D6-only logic: place 6 maroons into the first 6 cells of the full\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:31:#      Fused logic: 6 maroons need only a 3x3 square, so the output keeps only\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:33:#      with maroon, leaves the remaining 3 cells green, and turns the removed\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:47:#    - \\\"moved maroons fill exactly the visible input container\\\" is invalid;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:70:#    - Walls remain external; maroons remain on floor in the input, so objects\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:75:#    - The only count-based step is human-visible: count the reachable maroons,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:92:#    - Assumption: there is at least one reachable maroon in accepted samples,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:94:#      Generator: chooses at least 5 reachable source maroons.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:221:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into a variable square container, then shrink that container when the moved count is too small.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:224:    - Orange floor contains optional magenta walls and scattered maroon (9) pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:228:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the square, traversing only floor and maroon cells, then rank reachable maroons by BFS distance with row-major tie-breaking.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:229:    - Move as many ranked maroons as possible, capped by the input square area. If that moved count is smaller than the input capacity, rebuild the destination as the smallest anchored square that can hold those moved maroons; otherwise keep the original square size.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:230:    - Clear the moved source maroons back to floor, fill the final square in row-major order with the moved maroons, and leave any unused cells inside that final square as green/red container cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:233:    - The visible input square is only an upper bound on capacity. The solver must first detect the whole anchored square, then count how many maroons are actually reachable, because that count determines whether the output stays full-size or collapses to a smaller square.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:244:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:245:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < 10**9]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:246:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:249:    moved_count = min(capacity, len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:250:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:moved_count]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D10/1/code.py:26:#     output_grid: 16x16 periodic lattice plus centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp of the glyph\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D10/1/code.py:45:#     looks like black square holes separated by orange lattice lines. The 6x6 maroon center stamp is unchanged.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D10/1/code.py:50:#     center_stamp: unchanged and still overlays maroon on top of either orange or black cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D10/1/code.py:61:#     - center overwrite with maroon: still safe because maroon is a dedicated overlay color and the center region\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D10/1/code.py:74:#       maroon = centered stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D10/1/code.py:111:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice whose orange/black roles are inverted, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D10/1/code.py:121:    - Tile the original 3x3 motif 2x2 into a centered 6x6 region and recolor the motif pixels to maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/38/code.py:34:#    orthogonally convex blue regions (rectangles, separated rectangles, L-shapes)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/10/code.py:15:#       - Input: a blue (1) L-shape sits below a red horizontal line.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D15/2/code.py:92:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 alternating lattice, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D15/2/code.py:103:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true cells to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:16:#    floor, magenta walls, and maroon tokens outside the block. The original task only erased chosen\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:17:#    reachable maroons and refilled the destination block. Here the same BFS ranking still chooses the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:19:#    the farthest reachable maroon distance. A shortest path from each collected source to the block is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:41:#    The generator never places maroons inside the destination block or on walls. Corridor branches stay\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:57:#    reachable maroons still fill the destination in distance order, the farthest reachable maroon sets\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:240:    Pull reachable maroon pixels into the central 3×3 block, stretch space around that block, and show teal transport routes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:243:    - The input still uses the original 11×11 vocabulary: orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and a fixed green 3×3 destination with one red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:244:    - Openings beside the destination lead into floor corridors; only maroons connected through those corridors are reachable.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:247:    - Flood-fill from passable cells adjacent to the destination, treating floor and maroon as passable, then sort reachable maroons by BFS distance and by row/column.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:248:    - Let the farthest reachable maroon distance be the expansion width; output a larger canvas formed by inserting that many floor rows and columns around the destination block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:249:    - Move the closest reachable maroons into the destination in row-major order, erase their source cells, and paint every floor cell on each chosen BFS route teal, including the stretched bridge through the inserted bands.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:252:    - The same connectivity-and-distance rule decides which maroons are collected, but solving the combo now requires two extra inferences: reconstructing predecessor paths for the trail, and remapping the whole scene into a larger coordinate system whose added width depends on the farthest reachable maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:267:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:268:    reachable = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < INF]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/50/code.py:270:    assert reachable, \\\"there must be at least one reachable maroon token\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/2/code.py:24:#     - output remains a 16x16 orange/black period-3 lattice with a centered 6x6 maroon stamp\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/2/code.py:52:#       The central maroon stamp still shows the original L orientation, so the relation between\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/2/code.py:66:#     - center stamping can still overwrite the lattice safely because the maroon layer is the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/2/code.py:74:#     - the 2x2 maroon stamp exposes the source glyph directly, letting a human compare stamp\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/2/code.py:77:#     - the task still uses three output colors only: black, orange, maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/2/code.py:79:#       legible because maroon cleanly overwrites orange/black cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/2/code.py:142:    - Repeat that orange/black phase tile across the 16x16 canvas, then stamp the original glyph tiled 2x2 in maroon at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D11/2/code.py:20:#     into a 2x2 maroon block, yielding a 6x6 coarse stamp\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D11/2/code.py:37:#   - the difference is human-visible in 2-3 examples because repeated seams disappear and contiguous 2x2 maroon blocks appear\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D11/2/code.py:41:#   - colors remain black/orange/maroon in the output; no new color mapping is introduced, so the only new inference is geometric\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D11/2/code.py:93:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a periodic orange lattice and stamp a magnified maroon version at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D11/2/code.py:103:    - Recolor the glyph to maroon and enlarge each of its pixels into a 2x2 solid block, producing a centered 6x6 stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:21:#    everything. So the reachable maroon set depends on both where the search is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:29:#    - There is no single floor color anymore, so erased maroons cannot be\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:178:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:179:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < INF]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:180:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:181:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:182:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:193:    Pull the nearest direction-reachable maroon tokens into the 3x3 target around the red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:206:    - Reachable maroon cells are ranked by directed distance, then by row and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:208:    - Each moved maroon is erased back to the stripe background color of its\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/13/code.py:216:    maroons can actually reach the target.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/0/code.py:20:#     color: any single non-{black, orange, maroon}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/0/code.py:23:#     - centered 6x6 maroon stamp made by tiling the input motif 2x2\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/0/code.py:24:#     - output uses black/orange/maroon only\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/0/code.py:40:#       maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/0/code.py:53:#     - stamp the maroon 6x6 motif last\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/0/code.py:76:#     layers in sequence before stamping maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/0/code.py:77:#   - Original final maroon overwrite remains valid and must stay last so the stamp is not\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/0/code.py:85:#   - The detail region is fixed to rows/cols 4..11 (an 8x8 square), and the maroon stamp\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/0/code.py:93:#     period, fine detail uses 2x2 repetition only in the center, and maroon remains the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/0/code.py:194:    Decode one 3x3 glyph into a two-stage tiled scene: a coarse background lattice, then a finer central overlay, then a maroon center stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/0/code.py:204:    - Tile the original 3x3 motif 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:40:#    Original output only moved reachable maroon tokens into the 3x3 target.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:42:#    maroons, but its hidden BFS footprint becomes visible: every reachable\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:44:#    unreachable maroon distractor turns blue(1). Example: if a maroon sits\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:45:#    behind a wall arm, original output left it maroon; new output recolors it\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:47:#    maroons are still removed, but their cells now become trail color rather\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:51:#    reachable path/background, 1 means rejected maroon. This is enough to make\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:60:#    It also cannot assume all non-moved maroons stay maroon: unreachable ones\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:69:#    connected region from the target openings, while rejected blue maroons sit\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:71:#    visible because only the closest reachable maroons are transferred into the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:82:#    non-empty unreachable floor, and at least one unreachable maroon so the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:240:    Move the nearest reachable maroon pixels into the center block, while exposing the reachability map.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:243:    - The board uses orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and a unique red center inside a 3x3 green destination block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:247:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells adjacent to the destination, using orange and maroon cells as the traversable medium.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:248:    - Sort reachable maroon tokens by BFS distance, then by row and column; move the closest ones into the destination in row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:249:    - In the output, every reachable floor location is recolored to the trail color, chosen source tokens disappear into that trail, and unreachable maroon tokens are recolored blue.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:252:    - The destination fill still depends on the same reachability-and-distance logic as the original task, but this variant also paints the whole reachable component and explicitly marks rejected maroons, turning the hidden flood-fill partition into visible evidence.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:266:    reachable_maroons = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:267:    unreachable_maroons = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:272:            reachable_maroons.append(item)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:274:            unreachable_maroons.append((int(r), int(c)))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:275:    reachable_maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:277:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(reachable_maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:278:    chosen_sources = {(r, c) for _, r, c in reachable_maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:284:    for r, c in unreachable_maroons:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/22/code.py:78:#   - 干扰组件只用短线、L 形、2x2 方块等简单非 '+' 结构，减少局部纹理冲突。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D8/0/code.py:58:#      \\\"irrelevant marker\\\" colors, and output colors remain black/orange/maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D8/0/code.py:125:    Recover the lone valid 3x3 contour code from a noisy orange field, then build the same 16x16 phase lattice and centered maroon stamp as in the base task.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D8/0/code.py:135:    - Tile the recovered 3x3 glyph 2x2 and stamp its true cells in maroon inside the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D7/1/code.py:123:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a 16x16 periodic lattice with the motif stamped in maroon at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D7/1/code.py:133:    - Fill the 16x16 canvas with that phase tile, then stamp a 2x2 maroon tiling of the glyph into the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:19:#   - Step 2 overwrites the centered coarse 2x2 block with maroon cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:22:#     orange coarse pixels expand to orange glyph tiles, and maroon coarse pixels expand to\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:23:#     maroon glyph tiles. The final canvas is therefore 18x18.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:26:#     orange/black lattice -> stamp a flat 6x6 maroon 2x2 repetition at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:28:#     place a coarse 2x2 maroon block -> recursively replace every non-black coarse cell by a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:50:#   - The expanded output assumes coarse pixels use only black/orange/maroon, which main()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:55:#   - The centered coarse 2x2 maroon block occupies rows 2..3 and cols 2..3 of the 6x6 macro\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:56:#     raster, yielding a centered 6x6 maroon-bbox in the 18x18 final output.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:67:#   - Colors remain structurally simple: orange marks phase-lattice cells, maroon marks the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:147:    - Build a coarse 6x6 lattice by tiling that phase tile and overwrite the centered coarse 2x2 block with maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:148:    - Expand each coarse pixel into a 3x3 child tile shaped like the input glyph: orange cells become orange glyph tiles, maroon cells become maroon glyph tiles, and black cells stay black.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:28:#    - 原题的 `maroons.sort()` 默认是最近优先；这里必须改成距离降序，否则 D3/0 不生效。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:35:#    - 生成器先在仅 floor 的距离图上选近层/远层候选，再把这些 floor 位置改成 maroon，\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:47:#    - 新规则不引入新的颜色种类，只重排已有 maroon / green / red 的出现位置。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:169:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:170:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:171:    return dest_cells, fill_slots, floor, maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:177:    dest_cells, fill_slots, floor, maroons = _analyze_grid(grid)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:180:        maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:182:        maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:185:    k = min(len(target_slots), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:186:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:199:    Move the farthest reachable maroon pixels into a checkerboard subset of the 3x3 block around the lone red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:202:    - The board is an orange floor with optional magenta walls and scattered maroon source pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:206:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination, walking only through floor or maroon cells, and keep only reachable maroon pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:208:    - Move the selected maroons into the destination's row-major odd positions only, which forms a checkerboard pattern; the even positions keep their original green/red contents.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:211:    - The walls still determine reachability, but the visible output now combines two independent cues: source removal prefers the outermost reachable maroons, and the target block only accepts them on alternating checkerboard cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/28/code.py:24:#     - 每个样例至少放 2 个假红装饰，且既可能是单点，也可能是短线/L 形，保证“同色干扰”\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/2/code.py:25:#     - centered 6x6 maroon stamp made by 2x2 tiling the 3x3 glyph\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/2/code.py:43:#       -> stamp the centered maroon 2x2 motif\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/2/code.py:55:#   - stamping must happen after erasing; otherwise the erase step would clip maroon pixels and blur the two-stage logic.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/2/code.py:61:#   - the output keeps only black/orange/maroon, so the new effect is silhouette-based and clean.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/2/code.py:63:#   - only two layers remain in the lattice region (orange on black), plus the central maroon stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/2/code.py:131:    - Erase the tiled lattice outside that window, then tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/0/code.py:17:#   shifts it by one column. The central 6x6 maroon stamp is unchanged.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/0/code.py:35:#   Phase shifts affect the whole background lattice while the central maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/0/code.py:95:    - Repeat that phase tile over a black 16x16 canvas using the chosen offset, then tile the original glyph 2x2 and recolor its true cells to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/14/code.py:146:    Key insight: The solver must recognize a broken rotationally symmetric cross from its asymmetric L-shaped fragment. Detection is done on the original input only, and each detected elbow is expanded to the unique full '+' centered at the same pixel.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:14:#    The original task used a centered 3x3 destination and maroon tokens scattered anywhere on floor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:16:#    Maroon sources are no longer interior speckles: every movable or distracting maroon lies on the outer border.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:19:#    which maroons qualify, but now the candidate pool itself is visibly \\\"edge only\\\" and strongly asymmetric.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:22:#    positional change from a few examples. Border-only maroons are a strong visual cue, and the wall layout uses\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:26:#    - Collectible maroons are filtered to border cells only; interior maroons, if present, are ignored as sources.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:30:#    The chosen centers keep the full 5x5 wall frame in-bounds. Walls, destination cells, and border maroons occupy\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:31:#    disjoint cell sets, and all source/distractor maroons are sampled only from floor border cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:33:#    In 2-4 examples, a solver can see that maroons only appear on the boundary and that the block sits off-center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:34:#    Which border maroons move is explained by visible corridors/openings rather than invisible bookkeeping.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:36:#    Each role has its own region: the 3x3 target, a magenta wall frame, and edge-only maroons. This avoids the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:39:#    No new color remapping is introduced. The only semantic change is positional: \\\"border maroons reachable through\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:184:    Move the nearest reachable border maroons into the off-center 3x3 block around the red pixel.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:188:    - Maroon source pixels appear only on the outer border of the grid; some border maroons may be cut off by walls.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:191:    - Find the unique red cell, take its surrounding 3x3 as the destination, then flood-fill outward through floor and maroon cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:192:    - Only border maroons reached by that flood-fill are candidates; sort them by BFS distance, then row, then column.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:196:    - The asymmetry comes from two places at once: candidate maroons live only on the border, and the target block sits closer to\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:197:      some borders than others. Visible wall barriers decide which border sides can actually contribute maroons.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:238:    maroons = []\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:243:            maroons.append((int(dist[r, c]), r, c))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:244:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:246:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:247:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:17:#      maroon stamp made by tiling the 3x3 glyph 2x2.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:33:#      leaving the centered maroon stamp unchanged.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:44:#    - The centered 6x6 maroon stamp in output is unchanged and cannot conflict with generation.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:50:#    - The output still has only two clean layers: periodic background and centered maroon stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:53:#    - Colors are unchanged from the original task: orange/black for the lattice and maroon for\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:91:    Turn the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice whose phase is shifted by the glyph placement, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:102:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/0/code.py:18:#      2. a centered 6x6 maroon stamp made by tiling the original 3x3 glyph 2x2\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/0/code.py:31:#                  more separated lattice. The center 6x6 maroon H-stamp is unchanged.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/0/code.py:61:#    - Only two layers exist in the output: the periodic orange/black lattice and the central maroon stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/0/code.py:66:#      Output still uses only black, orange, and maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/0/code.py:112:    Read the 3x3 contour glyph as both a phase-shape code and a period code, then build the repeated lattice with the glyph stamped in maroon at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/0/code.py:123:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon inside the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:23:#    - Reachability still uses 4-neighbor BFS through floor/maroon cells, but a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:24:#      maroon is moved only if it lies within the number of BFS layers unlocked\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:27:#      old: fixed 3x3, all reachable maroons compete for 9 cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:28:#      new 4x4: only distance<=1 maroons are moved, and output becomes 6x6.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:29:#      new 5x5: distance<=2 maroons are moved, and output becomes 9x9.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:34:#    - Generators force at least one moved maroon on the outermost unlocked BFS\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:35:#      layer and at least one farther reachable maroon that remains, so the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:50:#    - Distractor maroons are sampled outside the final expanded square so they\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:55:#    - The output visibly shows a larger green/maroon square, revealing that the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:57:#    - Farther reachable maroons remain on the floor, so the growth cutoff is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:62:#    - Walls and leftover maroons remain outside the final container, avoiding\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:72:#    - Each accepted grid must have at least one moved maroon on the last growth\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:73:#      layer and at least one still-reachable maroon beyond that layer.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:82:#    - Assumption: leftover maroons outside the moved set are outside the final\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:199:    Grow a variable-size square container outward and move only the maroons reached within its growth depth.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:202:    - Orange floor contains optional magenta walls and scattered maroon (9) pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:206:    - Flood-fill through floor and maroon cells from the square's outside edge, measuring 4-neighbor BFS distance.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:207:    - The square expands by a size-dependent number of rings: 4x4 grows by 1 ring, 5x5 grows by 2 rings. Move only the maroons within those unlocked BFS layers.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:208:    - Erase moved maroons to floor, replace the expanded square by green, then write the collected maroons into that expanded square in row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:225:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:226:    chosen = [(d, r, c) for d, r, c in maroons if d <= rounds]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:18:#       color: any single color except black(0), orange(7), maroon(9)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:23:#     stamp: the original 4x4 motif tiled 2x2 into an 8x8 maroon center block\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:24:#     colors_used: black(0), orange(7), maroon(9)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:36:#        output       = repeat that 3x3 tile, then stamp a 6x6 maroon 2x2 copy.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:40:#        output       = repeat that 4x4 tile on 16x16, then stamp an 8x8 maroon 2x2 copy.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:76:#      maroon stamp. No extra markers or overlapping annotation channels are added.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:81:#      Output colors stay restricted to black/orange/maroon, exactly as in the base task.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:168:    Decode the colored 4x4 contour motif into a 16x16 period-4 lattice and stamp a centered maroon 2x2 copy of that motif.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:178:    - Tile the original 4x4 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 8x8 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:27:#      6x6 maroon stamp made by tiling the 3x3 glyph 2x2.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:54:#    - Center stamping still assumes the lattice can be overwritten by maroon on motif\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:64:#    - Humans can see the change directly: outside the maroon center, orange cells now\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:72:#      centered maroon overlay. The overlay is confined to a 6x6 block, so most of the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:75:#    - Output colors stay limited to black(0), orange(7), and maroon(9). Orange marks the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:77:#      maroon marks the centered 2x2 glyph stamp. This structured reuse keeps the rule\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:103:    Turn the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice that uses the glyph itself as the orange phase tile, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:113:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:19:#   with a red center and green ring, orange floor, magenta walls, and many maroon tokens outside.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:22:#   2. Among reachable maroons, the chosen movers are ordered by Euclidean distance to the block center,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:31:# - Important difference from the original generator: if there are <= 9 reachable maroons, every reachable\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:33:#   reachable maroons so the 9-cell capacity forces a visible keep-vs-move selection.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:37:# - Use 10-14 reachable maroons and at most 0-3 unreachable distractors. This is enough to expose the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:48:#   Broken by D3/2. The new solver must compute reachability by flood-fill but rank selected maroons by\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:50:# - Original assumption hidden in the old generator: reachable maroon count can be 2-9.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:52:#   The new generator guarantees more reachable maroons than capacity.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:57:# - The destination block is fixed at rows 4-6 and cols 4-6; source maroons are placed only on floor cells\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:64:# - Because only 9 of 10-14 reachable maroons move, some reachable maroons remain outside in the output.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:73:# - Distractors are limited and optional. Most of the visual signal comes from the reachable maroons around\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:78:# - The green ring must stay passable; generator never replaces it with walls or maroons in the input.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:169:def _reachable_maroons_from_center(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], np.ndarray, list[tuple[int, int]]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:172:    maroons = [\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:177:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:178:    return center, dist, maroons\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:182:    center, _dist, maroons = _reachable_maroons_from_center(grid)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:183:    ranked = sorted(maroons, key=lambda rc: (_euclid2(center, rc), rc[0], rc[1]))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:188:    _center, dist, maroons = _reachable_maroons_from_center(grid)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:189:    ranked = sorted(maroons, key=lambda rc: (int(dist[rc[0], rc[1]]), rc[0], rc[1]))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:197:    maroons = [\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:202:    ranked = sorted(maroons, key=lambda rc: (int(dist[rc[0], rc[1]]), rc[0], rc[1]))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:222:    center, dist_center, reachable = _reachable_maroons_from_center(grid)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:247:    Move the selected reachable maroons into the centered 3x3 block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:255:      and maroon cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:256:    - Keep only the reachable maroons, then rank them by Euclidean distance to the block center, breaking ties\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:258:    - Move up to nine ranked maroons into the destination block in row-major order and erase only those sources.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D3/2/code.py:16:#     - 原逻辑：若训练源图里有两个分开的 L 形，global fill 会跨整个 6x6 的行列范围补点，可能把两个对象混在一起。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D14/2/code.py:26:#      stamp one maroon 2x2 motif at the center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D14/2/code.py:29:#      and the later bbox layer second -> stamp the union of the two 2x2 motifs in maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D14/2/code.py:46:#      maroon \\\"stamp\\\" idea is preserved by taking the union after 2x2 tiling.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D14/2/code.py:55:#    There are only two lattice colors plus black and the single maroon center stamp. The\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D14/2/code.py:151:    Decode two colored contour glyphs into stacked periodic lattices, then seal their combined motif as a centered maroon stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D14/2/code.py:161:    - Composite the two repeated layers so the later bbox in row-major order overwrites the earlier one, then stamp the 2x2-tiled union of both glyphs in maroon inside the centered 6x6 window.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/12/code.py:32:       an L-shaped red marker. Its corner is the anchor, and the payload reflects\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/12/code.py:481:    - L-shaped red marker -> diagonal reflection\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:18:#    - Replace the single maroon source class with 2-3 token colors drawn from a small fixed\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:25:#        distance order      = [(d0,blue), (d1,maroon), (d2,blue), (d3,yellow)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:26:#        grouped order       = [(blue,d0), (blue,d2), (yellow,d3), (maroon,d1)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:28:#      Original task would have written a uniform maroon row-major prefix; this combo instead\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:39:#    - `passable = {floor, 9}` breaks because movable tokens are no longer all maroon; now every\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:46:#    - Original floor inference from \\\"the only other color is maroon\\\" is unsafe with multi-color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D16/1/code.py:141:    - Fill a 16x16 canvas by tiling that phase with the legend-selected colors, then stamp a 2x2 maroon copy of the glyph in the centered 6x6 region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/0/code.py:96:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 into a 6x6 pattern and recolor its true cells to maroon at the exact center of the output.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:18:#   - Replace the old \\\"all reachable maroons are already passable, then sort once by distance\\\" rule\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:21:#       2. A maroon cell is collected when it sits on the current BFS frontier, i.e. it is 4-neighbor\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:23:#       3. Collected maroons turn into floor, so the reachable floor region expands.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:24:#       4. Repeat layer by layer until the 3x3 destination is full or no frontier maroons remain.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:25:#   - This makes maroon cells behave like removable gate tokens instead of already-open corridor cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:29:#       * Treat floor and maroon as passable from the start.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:31:#       * Sort every reachable maroon by raw BFS distance and move the closest ones.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:34:#       * Just beyond that opening, one maroon gate blocks access to the first annulus.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:35:#       * After removing that gate, the first annulus becomes reachable; maroons sitting in that annulus\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:39:#       * Reachability is no longer static. A farther maroon that is \\\"close\\\" under the original solver\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:42:#         gate maroon that must be peeled away before the next depth becomes reachable.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:48:#     maroons, so the solver must reason about both partial final-layer filling and nested unlocking.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:49:#   - The generator prefers far-from-entry maroons in inner annuli and near-entry maroons in outer annuli,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:57:#   - The original assumption \\\"maroon is globally passable\\\" is no longer valid. The combo solver must BFS\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:68:#   - Gate maroons are reserved on floor cells known to be inside bounds and not in the destination block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:69:#   - Source maroons are sampled from disjoint floor-cell candidate sets; distractors, when used, are sampled\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:73:#   - A human sees nested magenta frames with different opening sides, plus maroons clustered by depth.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:74:#   - The output effect is not just \\\"take the closest maroons\\\": inner gate tokens disappear first, then the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:346:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:347:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:348:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:349:    chosen = [(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[: len(dest_cells)]]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:375:    Pull maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the red center by unlocking the nested frames layer by layer.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:384:    - At each step, collect every maroon that lies on the current BFS frontier, in row-major order; the collected maroons become floor, which may open the next annulus.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:385:    - Continue outward layer by layer until the destination block is full or no frontier maroons remain, then place the collected maroons into the destination in row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:387:    Key insight: The nested magenta frames do not just filter static reachability. Their openings create a sequence of locked annuli, and maroon gates must be removed in BFS layers before farther maroons can even become candidates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/2/code.py:30:#      centered 6x6 maroon mark. Empty input cells map to all-black panels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/2/code.py:59:#    - Panels are spatially disjoint, separated by black gutters, and maroon only appears\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/2/code.py:158:    - In the output mosaic, fill the corresponding 8x8 panel with that orange/black tile and stamp a 2x2 tiling of the glyph in maroon at the panel center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:22:#     stamp: still a 2x2 tiling of the original glyph recolored to maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:31:#     plus -> decode phase -> always build a 16x16 lattice -> stamp the 6x6 maroon motif at rows 5..10, cols 5..10\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:33:#     plus -> decode phase -> build a 12x12 lattice -> center the same 6x6 maroon stamp at rows 3..8, cols 3..8\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:34:#     H    -> decode phase -> build an 18x18 lattice -> center the same 6x6 maroon stamp at rows 6..11, cols 6..11\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:52:#   - Output placement is always legal because every canvas size is square and >= 12, while the maroon stamp is fixed at 6x6.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:57:#   - The new rule is visible because the whole output frame expands or shrinks by glyph type while the central maroon motif stays 6x6.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:61:#   - Only three output colors remain: black, orange, maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:62:#   - The maroon stamp stays in a dedicated centered block, separated from the outer lattice by several cells on every size class.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:120:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a glyph-sized periodic lattice and place a centered maroon stamp of the motif.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:130:    - Fill that square canvas by tiling the decoded phase tile, then center a 2x2 maroon tiling of the original glyph on top.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:17:#    The original task only moved reachable maroon tokens into the fixed 3x3 destination and erased\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:22:#    - within that region, the actual predecessor chains that carry chosen maroons back to the target\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:35:#      chosen maroons back into floor. That no longer holds; reachable background must also change.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:40:#      reachable branch with no maroon source, so some explored cells remain yellow-only.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:45:#    maroons are placed on isolated floor pockets outside the corridor network.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:48:#    untouched walls stay magenta, unreachable pockets stay orange/maroon, all reachable background\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:57:#    carries collected maroons\\\". The generator enforces both roles in every accepted sample.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:180:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:181:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < INF]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:182:    maroons.sort()\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:184:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:185:    chosen = [(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:206:    Gather reachable maroon pixels into the central 3x3 block and visualize both the explored region and the transport routes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:209:    - The board contains orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and a fixed green 3x3 destination with one red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:210:    - Passable openings beside the destination lead into corridor-like floor regions; isolated floor pockets may hold unreachable distractor maroons.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:213:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination, treating orange floor and maroon tokens as passable.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:214:    - Rank reachable maroons by flood-fill distance, then by row and column; the closest ones fill the destination in row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:215:    - In the output, every reachable floor cell becomes yellow to show the explored background, while the actual floor cells on each chosen source-to-destination parent chain are recolored teal; chosen source maroons themselves disappear back to orange.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:218:    - The fill order is still controlled by reachability and distance, but the fused variant exposes two nested BFS products: the full reachable background region and the narrower subset of floor cells that lie on the transport routes of the collected maroons.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:20:#     old_center_rule: every true pixel of the 2x2 tiled glyph became maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:21:#     new_center_rule: maroon appears only where the tiled glyph overlaps the 3-period lattice seams\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:25:#     variant: for plus, only the 8 true pixels on rows {0,3} or cols {0,3} inside that 6x6 box become maroon\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:29:#       which would collapse the stamp to zero maroon pixels\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:101:    - Tile the 3x3 glyph 2x2 into the centered 6x6 box, but recolor to maroon only where those glyph pixels also lie on the box's period-3 seam rows or seam columns.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:126:    maroon_mask = center & seam_mask\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:130:    out[r0 : r0 + center.shape[0], c0 : c0 + center.shape[1]][maroon_mask] = Color.MAROON\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:149:    maroon_count = int((center == Color.MAROON).sum())\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:150:    if maroon_count <= 0:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:19:#      keep only reachable maroons, sort them by BFS step distance, then place\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:20:#      the chosen maroons into the 3x3 block in row-major order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:23:#      1. Mark every reachable maroon with its BFS reachability information.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:24:#      2. Re-sort those marked maroons by Euclidean distance to the red center.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:34:#      only when there are more than 9 reachable maroons.  Then the top-9 set\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:35:#      itself can differ, changing which scattered maroons disappear.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:38:#    - The generator forces >9 reachable maroons and requires the Euclidean\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:48:#    - \\\"only orange floor and maroon are passable\\\": unchanged.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:56:#    - Generator places maroons only on floor cells, never inside the 3x3 block\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:59:#      sources, leftover reachable maroons, and distractors never overlap.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:62:#    - A human can see the distinction because some maroons that are geometrically\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:64:#      farther maroon that stays behind.  The walls provide the visible reason\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:71:#      red center, maroon tokens.  No extra marks are added.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:73:#      barrier network, scattered maroons.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:138:def _mark_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dest_cells: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:147:def _sort_marked_maroons(marked: list[tuple[int, int, int]], center_r: int, center_c: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:165:    Pull reachable maroons into the central 3x3 block, but separate marking,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:175:    - Phase 1 marks every maroon that is reachable through 4-connected floor or\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:176:      maroon cells starting from passable cells adjacent to the target block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:177:    - Phase 2 reorders only those marked maroons by Euclidean distance to the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:179:    - Phase 3 moves the first nine (or fewer) maroons from that Euclidean list:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:185:      longer depends on corridor length.  A maroon that is geometrically close\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:186:      to the center can outrank a path-shorter maroon if walls force a detour.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:195:    marked = _mark_reachable_maroons(grid, dest_cells)   # phase 1: mark\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:196:    ordered = _sort_marked_maroons(marked, cr, cc)       # phase 2: sort\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:21:#     - the old output had one 6x6 maroon stamp at the center\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:32:#     - place one 6x6 maroon plus-stamp at center top-left (5,5)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:36:#     - place the same 6x6 maroon plus-stamp four times at the quadrant-style slot origins\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:39:#     - the maroon foreground is no longer a single central event; it forms a regular 2x2 arrangement\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:59:#   - four maroon copies are obvious in 2-3 examples even when the glyph is symmetric\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:62:#   - maroon only overlays the phase lattice and never another stamp\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:65:#   - colors remain structurally simple: orange/black lattice plus maroon stamps\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:117:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a 16x16 periodic lattice with the motif stamped multiple times in maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:127:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph into a 6x6 stamp and place that maroon stamp at every slot of a regular 2x2 stamp lattice.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/4/code.py:14:      in the center window with fixed maroon(9). This variant transfers the visible input\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/4/code.py:20:    - Original behavior at the last step: center glyph pixels become maroon regardless of\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/4/code.py:60:      maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/4/code.py:61:    - Excluding maroon ensures generated samples do not collapse back to the original fixed\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/4/code.py:62:      maroon behavior, so the D4 change stays observable.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:20:#        source task: center 6x6 receives a 2x2 maroon tiling of the glyph\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:21:#        this variant: center 6x6 is forced to pure black, and one 3x3 maroon copy of\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:24:#        old flow  : decode plus -> periodic lattice -> maroon plus tiled at center\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:26:#                    -> stamp maroon plus at (0,0), (0,13), (13,0), (13,13)\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:33:#      corners carry the same maroon glyph. This is easy to compare across examples.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:38:#    - The old code assumed the only maroon overlay lived in a centered 6x6 block made by\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:53:#      black, and the maroon glyph migrates to all four corners. Because the lattice still\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:58:#      center, maroon stamps only in corners. No region carries multiple competing marks.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:61:#    - Colors remain black/orange/maroon only in the output. Maroon still signals the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:108:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice whose center becomes a black void and whose corners carry maroon glyph stamps.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:118:    - Erase the centered 6x6 zone to pure black, then stamp one maroon copy of the glyph into each of the four 3x3 corners.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:178:    # corner must contain at least one maroon pixel from the glyph stamp.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/14/code.py:50:#    - Large black foreground objects remain simple bands / rectangles / L-shapes so that the new\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D4/3/code.py:21:#     - Source motif: a 2x2 logical L-shape with exactly 3 foreground cells, one of them red.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D4/3/code.py:31:#         so the target quadrant shows three copies arranged in the same L-shape, each copy itself\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D4/3/code.py:53:#     - The L-shaped 2x2 logical motif guarantees visible holes/gaps, so the result is not mistaken for\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D4/3/code.py:237:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return a 2x2 logical L-shape with one red cell and two distinct extra colors.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:67:     1. the mover is visibly L-shaped rather than square;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:69:     3. the red goal is a larger docking frame with an L-shaped blue notch, and reachable outputs keep that frame\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:28:     3. The destination is a red docking frame whose inner cavity is an L-shaped blue notch\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D15/1/code.py:14:#    这个变体把单像素替换成 3x3 的同色 L 形记号；颜色仍然代表调色板颜色，但排序距离不再默认从最近边界测，\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:5:# 编码的小型 L 形图例，同色图例指示该颜色阻挡对应的转向偏好（CCW 或 CW）。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:12:#      其中 3 个同色像素构成一个 L 形符号：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:20:#      之一为真；本题中两者都为真，若底边颜色 4 的 L 形是 CCW，则转到上口，否则转到下口。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:48:#    - 每个图例条目就是一个 2x2 的单色 L 形，背景仍是原背景色 7；不会引入额外装饰噪声。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:60:#    - 假设 B：每个图例颜色在底边形成一个 4 连通、3 像素、2x2 bbox 的 L 形。生成器严格保证。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:116:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Read 2x2 bottom-edge L-shape symbols as color -> {ccw,cw}.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:23:    - Original: two L-shaped outside pieces could never exist, because two L-shaped holes were forbidden.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:24:    - Variant: two L-shaped holes may both exist. One hole touches a red wall marker, the other touches blue.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D1/0/code.py:34:    - 原逻辑：两个 L 形洞分别对应红/绿两个外部 L 形 piece。solver 先枚举每个 piece 的所有 D4 变体，\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D1/0/code.py:36:    - 变体逻辑：两个 L 形洞的洞边墙像素分别染成红/绿。solver 先看到“红洞边 -> 红 piece、绿洞边 -> 绿 piece”，\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D9/2/code.py:17:#     - 例：原任务里 3 格 L 形洞会变成 2x2 或 3x3 块拼出的 L 形精灵。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D10/0/code.py:19:#    8-neighbor depth differ. Example: in an L-shaped region, a cell tucked behind a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D1/4/code.py:31:    - 例子：frame 内有两个面积都为 4 的洞，左边是 L 形，右边是 1×4 横条。\\n/home/lix