/seed56627177/6/codegen_prompts/6.md:287:    \"jigsaw\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed165869686/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_105325/1_2.log:192:Assemble scattered jigsaw pieces into a rectangle, recoloring each by a legend sprite's color map.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed165869686/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_105325/1_2.log:204:Key insight: The legend piece doubles as both a jigsaw piece and a color key — its internal k×k palette assigns colors by spatial quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed165869686/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_105325/1_2.log:220:    \"jigsaw\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed165869686/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_105325/1_2.log:2195:    Assemble scattered jigsaw pieces into a rectangle, recoloring each by a legend sprite's color map.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed165869686/_codegen_logs/continue_20260619_141311/13_1.log:3064:Assemble scattered jigsaw sprites around a central yellow anchor by pairing red connector pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed165869686/_codegen_logs/continue_20260619_141311/13_1.log:3076:Key insight: Red pixels act as jigsaw pegs — each must match exactly one counterpart, and the assembly order is determined by which unpaired connectors remain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210621_gpt54_high_missing/1__codegen_prompts__3.log:14:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed56627177/1/prompt.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\\n\\n每个参考题描述包含：\\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\n\\n参考题目如下：\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"1\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"5ecac7f7\\\" lines=\\\"23-36\\\">\\n<description>\\nCombine the left, middle, and right ordered objects from three separated panels.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The grid is three HxH panels separated by one-cell vertical separator bars.\\n- The background is the dominant color, and each panel contains exactly three same-color 4-connected foreground objects.\\n\\nRule\\n- Build a new HxH background canvas.\\n- From the left panel copy its leftmost object, from the middle panel copy its middle object, and from the right panel copy its rightmost object.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The separator bars create three aligned layers, and the panel's own left-to-right object order selects which object survives in the merged output.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"878187ab\\\" lines=\\\"10-24\\\">\\n<description>\\nReplace the scattered foreground markers with a bottom-left count rectangle whose two corner diagonals encode the marker counts.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- A background grid with exactly two foreground colors used as scattered marker pixels.\\n- The two foreground colors have distinct pixel counts.\\n\\nRule\\n- Ignore marker positions and use only the two foreground counts.\\n- Make a 16-by-16 background canvas, fill a bottom-left red rectangle whose height is the smaller count and width is the larger count.\\n- Paint yellow pixels along the two rising 45-degree diagonals from the rectangle's bottom-left and bottom-right corners.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The marker colors and positions vary between examples; their counts alone determine the output rectangle dimensions.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"3\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"981571dc\\\" lines=\\\"6-19\\\">\\n<description>\\nReconstruct a 4-way symmetric mosaic by filling missing (black) pixels.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- A colored grid exhibiting bilateral symmetry along both a vertical and a horizontal axis.\\n- Some pixels are erased to color 0 (black), creating gaps in the pattern.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Infer the vertical and horizontal reflection axes from the visible (non-zero) pixels.\\n- For each black pixel, recover its color from the mirrored position across either axis or both.\\n- When multiple mirrors yield candidates, use the majority color.\\n\\nKey insight: The reflection axes are not given — they must be deduced from the surviving pixels by finding the axes that best preserve the existing symmetry.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"4\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"f560132c\\\" lines=\\\"259-273\\\">\\n<description>\\nAssemble scattered jigsaw pieces into a rectangle, recoloring each by a legend sprite's color map.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most common color.\\n- Several monochrome non-bg sprites (the \\\"pieces\\\"), scattered across the grid.\\n- One sprite is the legend: it contains a multi-color k×k patch (typically 2×2) encoding output colors.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Tile all pieces (rotations/reflections allowed) into a tight rectangle with no gaps.\\n- The legend's k×k color patch defines a spatial color map over the rectangle.\\n- Each piece is recolored to the legend-map color corresponding to its position in the assembled rectangle.\\n\\nKey insight: The legend piece doubles as both a jigsaw piece and a color key — its internal k×k palette assigns colors by spatial quadrant.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"5\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"5a719d11\\\" lines=\\\"44-59\\\">\\n<description>\\nWithin each horizontal pair of two-color panels, swap the motif masks and recolor each pasted mask with the source panel's base color.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- A separator color forms full blank rows and at least one full blank column.\\n- The non-separator area is split into row bands, each containing exactly two same-shaped rectangular panels.\\n- Each panel has a dominant base color and one minority motif color.\\n\\nRule:\\n- For every row band, clear each panel to its own base color.\\n- Paste the right panel's motif mask into the left panel using the right base color.\\n- Paste the left panel's motif mask into the right panel using the left base color.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The motif colors themselves are distractors; only each motif's shape mask and the two panel base colors are exchanged.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"6\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"c9680e90\\\" lines=\\\"52-67\\\">\\n<description>\\nMove each mirrored bottom source pixel to the far end of its trail and redraw the top half as its reflection.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- A solid non-background row separates equal-height top and bottom halves.\\n- The top half has one marker color on the background.\\n- In the bottom half, exactly one color has positions that mirror the top markers across the separator, and the other color forms trails touching those source pixels.\\n\\nRule\\n- Identify the bottom source color by reflecting each bottom color into the top half and matching the top marker set.\\n- For every bottom source pixel, follow its unique 4-connected trail of the other bottom color to the trail endpoint.\\n- Clear the old top markers, bottom sources, and trails; place the source color at each endpoint and place the top marker color at the reflected endpoint.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The top half is only a mirror display of the bottom moving sources; the actual motion is encoded by the trail attached to each bottom source pixel.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"7\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"981add89\\\" lines=\\\"10-29\\\">\\n<description>\\nExtend each top-row control pixel downward as a vertical toggle ray in its own color.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\n- Non-background pixels on the top row are control pixels, each identifying\\n  one column and one ray color.\\n- Foreground regions below may intersect these control columns.\\n\\nRule:\\n- For every top-row control pixel, process the cells below it in the same\\n  column down to the bottom edge.\\n- A cell that already has the control color is erased to the background.\\n- Every other cell on that downward ray is painted with the control color.\\n- The top-row control pixels themselves remain unchanged.\\n\\nKey insight:\\nThe top row is a set of vertical ray launchers; each ray toggles only cells\\nmatching its own color and overwrites all other colors along that column.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"8\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"da515329\\\" lines=\\\"11-24\\\">\\n<description>\\nGrow four clockwise spiral wall paths from the tips of a teal cross.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = 0 (black). A single teal (8) cross centered in the grid.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Each arm tip launches a \\\"turtle\\\" heading 90° right of its outward direction.\\n- Movement priority: turn right > go straight > turn left (left only if not on border).\\n- Normal step = 2 cells; step right after a turn = 1 cell.\\n- Each new cell must have a 1-cell orthogonal gap from all existing walls except the predecessor.\\n\\nKey insight: The right-turn preference plus alternating 2/1 step lengths creates self-avoiding spirals that tile the grid with uniform spacing.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"9\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"14b8e18c\\\" lines=\\\"40-57\\\">\\n<description>\\nMark every complete square object with red pixels just outside its corners.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- A uniform background contains one or more monochrome 4-connected foreground objects.\\n- The relevant objects are square frames or filled squares: their bbox is square\\n  and all cells on the bbox border have the object's color.\\n- Non-square bars and incomplete fragments may also appear and are ignored.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Keep the input unchanged.\\n- For each complete square object, paint red on the two outside background\\n  pixels orthogonally adjacent to each of the square's four corners.\\n\\nKey insight: The transformation is not based on size or color; it selects\\nobjects whose bounding box is a complete square border and labels only their\\nexposed outer corner-adjacent cells.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"10\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"42f83767\\\" lines=\\\"23-39\\\">\\n<description>\\nExpand the lower color grid by replacing each pixel with its matching top stencil.\\n\\nInput structure\\nThe input has a top legend and a lower dense color grid, separated by blank rows.\\nThe legend contains left-to-right 2x2 color swatches and, to their right,\\nthe same number of square neutral-color stencil masks.\\n\\nRule\\nPair the swatches and stencil masks by left-to-right order. For every pixel in\\nthe lower color grid, paste the paired stencil mask as one output block,\\nrecoloring the mask pixels with that pixel's color and leaving mask holes as bg.\\n\\nKey insight\\nThe lower grid is not copied directly; it is an index grid whose colors select\\nthe stencil shape from the legend, so each input pixel becomes one square block.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"11\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"f3e14006\\\" lines=\\\"21-39\\\">\\n<description>\\nBuild the woven rectangle determined by the two marked cells on each crossed bar.\\n\\nInput structure\\nA black-background grid contains one long horizontal bar and one long vertical bar.\\nEach bar has a dominant base color and exactly two same-colored marker pixels.\\n\\nRule\\nThe horizontal marker pair gives the output column span.  From the horizontal bar\\nrow, walk toward the farther vertical marker; rows and columns alternate every\\nother cell.  Even step/even offset cells use the horizontal marker color until\\nthe nearer vertical marker is reached, then use the vertical marker color.\\nOdd row steps use the horizontal base on marker columns and the original\\ncrossing color on spacer columns.  Spacer columns on even row steps use the\\nvertical base, except at the switch row where they use the crossing color.\\n\\nKey insight\\nThe original cross cell records which base color wins at base/base lattice\\ncrossings; the nearer vertical marker is the color-switch boundary.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed165869686/_codegen_logs/continue_20260619_141311/2_6.log:31:<new_puzzle index=\"6\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed165869686/_codegen_logs/continue_20260619_141311/6_6.log:31:<new_puzzle index=\"6\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed287049989/8/codegen_prompts/4.md:298:Assemble scattered jigsaw pieces into a rectangle, recoloring each by a legend sprite's color map.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed287049989/8/codegen_prompts/4.md:310:Key insight: The legend piece doubles as both a jigsaw piece and a color key — its internal k×k palette assigns colors by spatial quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed287049989/8/codegen_prompts/4.md:326:    \"jigsaw\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/14/codegen_prompts/6.md:11:<new_puzzle index=\"6\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed287049989/8/codegen_prompts/6.md:11:<new_puzzle index=\"6\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1967842053/2/codegen_prompts/6.md:11:<new_puzzle index=\"6\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210621_gpt54_high_missing/12__codegen_prompts__1.log:30:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_15\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed56627177/12/des.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：根据每个封闭区域内散落标记点的颜色，将该区域的边框重绘为标记点颜色，同时将标记点替换为边框原色。\\n- `Input structure`：背景为主色调（如 azure）。网格中有若干由不同颜色绘制的闭合矩形边框（如 red、green、maroon），每个矩形边框内部散布着若干单像素标记点，标记点颜色与所在矩形的边框颜色不同，但同一矩形内所有标记点颜色相同。不同矩形内的标记点颜色各不相同。矩形之间不重叠、不相邻。\\n- `Rule`：对每个闭合矩形边框，找到其内部所有标记点的颜色（同一矩形内标记点颜色唯一）。将该矩形的整条边框重绘为标记点的颜色，同时将所有标记点的像素替换为该矩形原来的边框颜色。背景像素保持不变。\\n- `Key insight`：边框颜色和内部标记点颜色发生互换——解题者需要先识别每个封闭边框与其内部标记点之间的配对关系，再执行颜色交换。表面看似简单的颜色替换，关键在于正确判定\\\"哪些标记点属于哪个边框\\\"这一归属关系。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：将网格中每个多色精灵按其内部颜色层数进行\\\"剥洋葱\\\"式分解，从外到内逐层提取轮廓并按从左到右的顺序排列在输出网格中。\\n- `Input structure`：背景为 black。网格中有若干个独立的多色精灵（互不接触），每个精灵由 2 到 4 种颜色组成，呈同心嵌套结构——最外层是一种颜色，向内每层换一种颜色，类似靶心图案（但形状不一定是矩形，可以是不规则的 4-连通区域，只要每层完整包裹内层即可）。每个精灵的层数可能不同。\\n- `Rule`：对每个精灵，从最外层开始逐层\\\"剥离\\\"——第一层是精灵最外圈像素构成的轮廓（即与背景 4-连通相邻的像素），第二层是去掉最外层后新暴露的外圈像素，依此类推，直到最内层核心。将每一层单独提取出来（保持其相对空间位置），按照从外到内的顺序从左到右排列在输出网格中，层与层之间用一列背景色分隔。每层只保留该层自身颜色的像素，其余位置为背景色。精灵之间的排列顺序按照它们在输入网格中从上到下、从左到右的出现顺序，精灵之间用两列背景色分隔。\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先识别每个精灵的同心嵌套层级结构，再理解\\\"剥离\\\"的顺序是从外向内逐层提取轮廓。两个非显然的推理步骤：（1）判断哪些像素属于同一\\\"层\\\"（即当前最外圈），（2）理解输出中各层的排列顺序编码了原精灵的嵌套深度。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：在网格中找到由墙壁围成的若干房间，每个房间有一个彩色钥匙和一扇同色的门（墙壁缺口），将钥匙颜色填充到连接钥匙所在房间与同色门所在房间之间的走廊中。\\n- `Input structure`：背景为 black。grey 像素构成正交墙壁，将网格分隔成若干矩形房间和连接房间的窄走廊（宽度为 1 格）。每个房间内恰好有一个彩色单像素（钥匙），颜色各不相同（可能有 red、blue、green、yellow 等）。每个房间的墙壁上恰好有一个缺口（宽度 1 格），缺口处有一个与某个钥匙同色的像素（门）。钥匙颜色与其所在房间的门颜色不同，但与另一个房间的门颜色相同。走廊只有 black 像素，连接各个房间的缺口。\\n- `Rule`：（1）匹配：每把钥匙与同色的门配对。（2）路径填充：从钥匙所在房间的缺口出发，沿走廊找到通向配对门所在房间的唯一路径（走廊网络中任意两个房间之间只有唯一路径，即树状拓扑）。将该走廊路径上的所有 black 像素填充为钥匙的颜色。（3）钥匙原位置设为 black，门像素保持不变，墙壁保持不变，房间内部其余位置保持不变。\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要完成两层推理：首先通过颜色匹配建立钥匙-门的配对关系（钥匙不在自己门所在的房间里，而在另一个房间），然后理解走廊路径的填充规则——走廊是树状结构所以路径唯一。颜色匹配是跨房间的间接关联，走廊路径填充则需要识别墙壁定义的拓扑连接结构。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：网格中有若干形状各异的单色精灵，每个精灵旁边有一个由相同颜色绘制的小 L 形箭头指示翻转方式；将每个精灵按箭头编码的轴进行镜像翻转。\\n- `Input structure`：背景为主色调（如 azure）。网格中有若干 4-连通的单色精灵，每个精灵的颜色互不相同。每个精灵的某一侧（上、下、左或右）紧邻一个由同色像素组成的 3 像素 L 形箭头标记——箭头由一条 2 像素长的直线段加上末端垂直拐弯的 1 像素构成，直线段的一端紧贴精灵边缘，另一端的拐弯像素向某个方向偏移。L 形标记与精灵之间无间隔（直接 4-连通相邻），且 L 形标记不与精灵的主体像素混淆（精灵主体像素数量至少为 5，L 形恰好 3 像素，且 L 形可通过其形状被唯一识别）。\\n- `Rule`：对每个精灵：（1）识别与精灵相邻的 L 形标记。L 形标记由 3 个同色像素组成，形成直角拐弯。（2）根据 L 形标记的朝向确定翻转轴——如果 L 形的拐弯像素相对于直线段在水平方向上偏移（即 L 形开口朝左或朝右），则执行左右镜像翻转（沿精灵竖直中轴翻转）；如果在垂直方向上偏移（即 L 形开口朝上或朝下），则执行上下镜像翻转（沿精灵水平中轴翻转）。（3）将精灵相对于自身包围盒中心执行对应的镜像翻转，翻转后位置不变。（4）删除 L 形标记（设为背景色）。背景保持不变。\\n- `Key insight`：解题者面临两层推理挑战：第一层是将 3 像素的 L 形从精灵主体中区分出来并解读其编码方式——L 形的开口方向并非指示移动方向，而是编码翻转轴的类型；第二层是正确执行精灵的原位镜像翻转。箭头编码方式的隐蔽性是本题的核心难点。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：网格被分割线分成四个面板，四个面板中的图案互补拼合为一个完整图案，同时每个面板角落的颜色提示块定义了一个跨面板的颜色重映射关系，输出为按此映射着色的完整拼合图案。\\n- `Input structure`：背景为 black。网格由 grey 的单像素宽分割线划分成 2×2 共四个大小相同的面板。四个面板共享同一个底层图案，但每个面板只显示该图案的一部分（即图案中的部分像素被擦除为背景色），且四个面板的可见部分互补——将四个面板叠加后恰好能恢复完整图案，任何像素位置至多在一个面板中可见。每个面板的可见像素全部是同一种颜色（如 red、blue、green、yellow，四个面板四种不同颜色）。此外，在每个面板的右下角有一个 1×1 的颜色提示块，其颜色等于另一个面板的可见像素颜色（四个提示块构成一个一一映射，无自映射）。\\n- `Rule`：（1）将四个面板的可见图案叠加，恢复出完整图案。（2）建立颜色映射：如果面板 A 的提示块颜色等于面板 B 的可见像素颜色，则在输出中，面板 B 贡献的所有像素用面板 A 的可见像素颜色绘制。（3）输出为单个面板大小的网格，包含完整图案，每个像素按上述映射着色。背景像素保持 black。提示块本身不出现在输出中。\\n- `Key insight`：本题包含三层推理：第一层是发现四个面板的图案互补，可以拼成一个完整图案；第二层是理解右下角提示块建立了面板间的颜色映射关系；第三层是正确应用这个映射——提示块指定的是\\\"谁的像素在输出中用我的颜色\\\"这一间接重定向关系。跨面板的间接颜色映射构成了本题的核心挑战。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：将网格中散布的碎片精灵按照边缘锯齿形状配对拼合成完整矩形，拼合后矩形内部的条纹方向决定该矩形在输出中是否旋转。\\n- `Input structure`：背景为 black。网格中有若干单色的不规则精灵，每个精灵的一侧边缘呈锯齿状（凹凸交替，凹凸深度为 1 像素），其余三侧边缘为直线。精灵颜色有若干种，每种颜色恰好有两个精灵。同色的两个精灵锯齿边缘互补——一个的凸出恰好填入另一个的凹陷，拼合后形成一个完整的矩形。每个精灵内部有 1 到 3 条平行的 grey 细线条纹（宽度 1 像素），条纹方向为水平或垂直，同一精灵内条纹方向一致。\\n- `Rule`：（1）按颜色配对精灵，将同色的两个精灵沿锯齿边缘拼合成一个完整矩形（通过平移使锯齿互补对齐，锯齿边缘相对放置）。（2）观察拼合后矩形内部 grey 条纹的方向：如果条纹是水平的，矩形保持原样不旋转；如果条纹是垂直的，将整个矩形顺时针旋转 90 度。（3）将所有拼合并可能旋转后的矩形按面积从小到大、从左到右排列在输出网格中，矩形之间用一列 black 分隔，底部对齐。grey 条纹在输出中保留。\\n- `Key insight`：本题有两层核心推理：第一层是通过锯齿边缘的互补形状识别配对关系并完成拼合——解题者需要发现同色精灵的锯齿边缘恰好吻合；第二层是发现内部条纹方向编码了旋转指令，条纹不是装饰而是操作信号。拼合机制与旋转编码的结合使得解题路径具有层次感。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：网格中的彩色连通区域各自包含一个异色\\\"种子\\\"像素，种子的颜色编码了生长方向；每个区域沿对应方向扩展边界直到受阻。\\n- `Input structure`：背景为 black。网格中有若干 4-连通的单色区域（颜色各不相同，可能包括 red、blue、green、yellow 等），区域之间互不接触，至少间隔 2 格背景。每个区域内部恰好有一个像素颜色与区域主色不同，这是\\\"种子\\\"像素。种子像素的颜色只会是以下四种之一：orange 表示向右生长、magenta 表示向下生长、azure 表示向左生长、maroon 表示向上生长。同一种种子颜色可以出现在多个区域中。\\n- `Rule`：（1）确定每个区域的种子颜色，对应生长方向：orange→右、magenta→下、azure→左、maroon→上。（2）将该区域沿指定方向逐列（或逐行）扩展：每次在区域朝该方向的整条边界外侧添加一列/行像素（颜色为区域主色）。（3）重复扩展，直到新添加的像素会与另一个区域的像素 4-连通相邻或触及网格边缘时停止（停在碰撞前一步，不添加会导致碰撞的那一列/行）。（4）种子像素在输出中被替换为区域主色（种子标记消失）。所有区域的扩展终止位置基于它们各自独立扩展到极限后的状态同时计算，不存在顺序依赖。\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要解决两层推理问题：第一层是建立种子颜色到生长方向的映射（需要从多个样例中归纳出四种种子颜色分别对应哪个方向，这不是直觉上显然的对应关系）；第二层是理解生长的机制——区域沿单一方向整列/行扩展直到受阻，且所有区域的扩展是同时判定的。种子颜色编码方向的映射关系需要跨样例归纳，是本题的核心隐蔽规律。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed165869686/_codegen_logs/continue_20260620_045458/13_6.log:25:<new_puzzle index=\"6\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed165869686/6/codegen_prompts/7.md:230:    \"jigsaw\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed165869686/6/codegen_prompts/6.md:11:<new_puzzle index=\"6\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed165869686/_codegen_logs/continue_20260620_045458/13_7.log:2552:Assemble scattered jigsaw sprites around a central yellow anchor by pairing red connector pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed165869686/_codegen_logs/continue_20260620_045458/13_7.log:2564:Key insight: Red pixels act as jigsaw pegs — each must match exactly one counterpart, and the assembly order is determined by which unpaired connectors remain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210621_gpt54_high_missing/12__codegen_prompts__5.log:35:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_17\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"rg -n \\\\\\\"new_puzzle index=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"|description|Input structure|Rule|Key insight\\\\\\\" /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed5662