象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\n\\n参考题目如下：\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"1\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"2c181942\\\" lines=\\\"7-21\\\">\\n<description>\\nAttach monochrome sprites to the matching sides of a central hollow square.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = background. A hollow NxN square (hub) with bg corners/interior and four differently-colored edges (top, bottom, left, right).\\n- 2-4 monochrome sprites scattered on the grid, each matching one hub edge color.\\n\\nRule:\\n- For each hub edge color, find the matching sprite outside the hub.\\n- Rotate the sprite (0/90/180/270°) so its contact edge has exactly N-2 contiguous cells aligned with the hub side, and the rotated sprite is mirror-symmetric along the contact-edge axis (UD for left/right, LR for top/bottom).\\n- Translate it to adjoin that hub side. \\n- Clear everything else to bg; output is hub + attached sprites only.\\n\\nKey insight: Each edge color uniquely pairs a sprite to a side; symmetry along the contact-edge axis disambiguates the correct rotation.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"221dfab4\\\" lines=\\\"6-19\\\">\\n<description>\\nPropagate a repeating striped pattern from a yellow border segment toward the opposite edge, recoloring foreground objects on certain stripes.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most common color. Foreground blobs of another color scattered in the interior.\\n- A short yellow (4) segment sits on one border edge.\\n\\nRule:\\n- From the yellow segment, march toward the opposite edge in steps of 2 cells, cycling colors Y, Y, G (4, 4, 3). The 1-cell gap between stripes is forced to bg.\\n- Yellow stripes paint only within the segment's span.\\n- Green stripes additionally recolor all non-bg pixels across the entire row/column to green.\\n\\nKey insight: Green stripes act as a \\\"flood\\\" that recolors existing objects on the full row/column, while yellow stripes are confined to the segment span.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"3\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"22208ba4\\\" lines=\\\"12-27\\\">\\n<description>\\nMove the repeated boundary color's rectangles one block inward while leaving singleton boundary rectangles in place.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The background is the most common color.\\n- Foreground objects are solid monochrome rectangles touching a grid corner.\\n- Exactly one foreground color appears as multiple separate 4-connected objects; other colors appear once.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Clear the multiple objects of the repeated color from their original positions.\\n- For each cleared rectangle, translate it away from the row and column border it touches by exactly its height and width.\\n- Keep singleton-color objects unchanged; overlapping translated rectangles of the same color merge.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- Multiplicity selects the moving color, and each boundary rectangle's touched edges determine its inward diagonal translation.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"4\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"2a28add5\\\" lines=\\\"8-22\\\">\\n<description>\\nPaint each pink control pixel as a teal horizontal bar whose reach equals the foreground counts on that row.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The grid has a dominant background color and one or more pink control pixels.\\n- Each marker row has exactly one pink pixel; all other non-background pixels\\n  in that row are counters.\\nRule\\n- Start from an all-background output grid.\\n- For each pink pixel, count non-background pixels strictly to its left and\\n  strictly to its right in the same row.\\n- Paint teal from c - left_count through c + right_count on that row.\\nKey insight\\n- The foreground pixels are not copied; only their counts on each side of\\n  each pink marker encode the teal bar length.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"5\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"c803e39c\\\" lines=\\\"31-40\\\">\\n<description>\\nExpand the second mask into a block grid by stamping the first mask with the two payload colors.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- A background grid has four panels separated by three full-height separator columns.\\n- The first two panels contain same-size binary masks; the last two contain solid same-size color squares.\\nRule\\n- Use the second mask as an outer layout. For each foreground cell in that outer mask, place a tile equal to the first mask, coloring its foreground with the first solid-square color and its background with the second solid-square color; outer background cells become all second solid-square color.\\nKey insight\\n- The output is the Kronecker product of the two binary masks, with the two right-hand panel colors providing the palette.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"6\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"269e22fb\\\" lines=\\\"46-60\\\">\\n<description>\\nComplete a visible crop into the shared 20x20 binary motif in its matching orientation.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The grid is a two-color rectangular crop of one rotation/reflection of the same 20x20 motif.\\n- One color is the motif foreground and the other color is the motif background.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Try each input color as the foreground mask.\\n- Match that mask against every possible window in every dihedral orientation of the motif.\\n- Repaint the uniquely matched full 20x20 motif with the matched foreground/background colors.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The examples are partial windows of one canonical binary pattern; the local crop is distinctive enough to identify the full orientation and offset.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"7\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"c4d067a0\\\" lines=\\\"9-23\\\">\\n<description>\\nComplete a grid of colored blocks to match a minimap legend in the top-left corner.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most common color.\\n- Top-left corner: a small sprite of single colored pixels forming a minimap pattern on a regular lattice.\\n- Main area: uniformly colored square blocks (NxN) arranged on a regular grid; some positions are empty (bg).\\n\\nRule:\\n- The legend pixels define a color pattern; each pixel's lattice position maps to a block position in the main grid via a fixed scale factor and offset.\\n- Existing colored blocks confirm the scale/offset alignment.\\n- For every legend pixel whose corresponding grid position is empty, place a new block of that color.\\n\\nKey insight: The top-left pixel pattern is a scaled-down minimap of the block layout; the mapping is inferred from blocks already present.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"8\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"800d221b\\\" lines=\\\"7-22\\\">\\n<description>\\nRecolor a path-network by adjacent seed regions.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most common color.\\n- Path color P forms a thin orthogonal network with a solid square hub (NxN).\\n- Seed colors appear in colored regions (non-bg, non-P) adjacent to path branches.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Infer P as the non-bg color whose largest component is most network-like.\\n- Find the largest solid k×k all-P square (the hub); exclude it from recoloring.\\n- Recolor each path branch to the seed-region color it touches most.\\n- Recolor the hub center pixel to the seed whose branches touch the hub most.\\n\\nKey insight: The hub stays uncolored; branches inherit color from adjacent seed regions by adjacency count.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"9\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"34cfa167\\\" lines=\\\"94-117\\\">\\n<description>\\nComplete a four-corner framed rectangle from one decorated anchor rectangle and its diagonal mate.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\n- Two same-color solid rectangular anchors of the same size sit on opposite\\n  diagonal corners, with the first anchor above-left of the second.\\n- The upper-left anchor has two one-cell-thick vertical control bars to its\\n  right and two one-cell-thick horizontal control bars below it.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Copy the anchor rectangle into the two missing corners of the implied\\n  larger rectangle.\\n- Repeat the right-side control bars horizontally between the left and right\\n  anchors, using their spacing as the period, and draw the outer top and\\n  bottom borders in the first right-control color.\\n- Repeat the below-side control bars vertically between the top and bottom\\n  anchors, using the same period, and draw the outer left and right borders\\n  in the first below-control color.\\n\\nKey insight: The small control bars are the first two ticks of two periodic\\nframe patterns; the diagonal anchor supplies the opposite corner and the\\nmissing two anchor copies.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"10\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"1e5d6875\\\" lines=\\\"26-45\\\">\\n<description>\\nPaint a recolored diagonal copy from each L triomino source object.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\n- The only foreground objects are 4-connected red and grey L triominoes,\\n  each occupying three pixels of a 2x2 box.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Grey L objects paint a yellow copy translated one diagonal step toward\\n  their missing 2x2 corner.\\n- Red L objects paint a green copy translated one diagonal step away from\\n  their missing 2x2 corner.\\n- Copies are clipped by the grid boundary; red-derived green copies are\\n  painted after grey-derived yellow copies where the projections collide.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The missing corner of each 2x2 L object identifies its diagonal axis, and\\n  the source color determines which side of that axis receives the copy.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"11\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"98c475bf\\\" lines=\\\"62-76\\\">\\n<description>\\nErase the complete interior glyph and expand each endpoint marker pair into its color's full glyph.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The grid is 20x20 with background inside two same-color full-height vertical frame bars.\\n- Inside the frame there is one complete color glyph and one or more other colors appearing only as two endpoint markers in the same row.\\n- Marker endpoints are always in the first and last interior columns.\\n\\nRule\\n- Keep the vertical frame unchanged.\\n- Erase any complete interior glyph.\\n- For each endpoint marker pair, use that marker color's learned glyph template and anchor its horizontal bar on the marker row.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- Color identifies which glyph shape to draw; the two endpoint pixels are not copied objects, they are anchors for reconstructing that color's full symbol.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"12\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"eee78d87\\\" lines=\\\"40-55\\\">\\n<description>\\nDecode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a 16x16 periodic lattice with the motif stamped in maroon at the center.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The grid is 6x6 with orange background and one non-orange color.\\n- The non-orange pixels have a tight 3x3 bbox containing one contour glyph.\\n- The glyph is one of the task's period-3 contour forms: plus, H, X, or four corners.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Decode the 3x3 glyph into the period-3 orange phase tile.\\n- Fill a black 16x16 canvas by repeating that orange phase tile.\\n- Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The colored object is not copied at its input location; it is a small contour code whose phase tells where orange appears in the repeated lattice.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"13\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"5dbc8537\\\" lines=\\\"10-23\\\">\\n<description>\\nFill rectangular cavities in a template shape by placing source sprites into matching holes.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most common color. A dominant \\\"base\\\" color forms a large frame/template with rectangular gaps.\\n- Small colored sprites sit outside the template region.\\n\\nRule:\\n- The base color (largest connected component excluding bg) defines the template bbox.\\n- Each rectangular hole inside the template matches exactly one outside sprite by size.\\n- Place each sprite into its matching cavity; output is the filled template bbox.\\n\\nKey insight: Sprite bounding boxes match cavity dimensions exactly — it's a jigsaw-fit puzzle where each piece has a unique slot.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"14\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"46c35fc7\\\" lines=\\\"21-34\\\">\\n<description>\\nRotate the colors around every 3x3 foreground ring, with corners and side-centers cycling in opposite directions.\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed165869686/12/codegen_prompts/6.md:11:<new_puzzle index=\"6\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210621_gpt54_high_missing/12__codegen_prompts__3.log:29:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed56627177/12/des.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：根据每个封闭区域内散落标记点的颜色，将该区域的边框重绘为标记点颜色，同时将标记点替换为边框原色。\\n- `Input structure`：背景为主色调（如 azure）。网格中有若干由不同颜色绘制的闭合矩形边框（如 red、green、maroon），每个矩形边框内部散布着若干单像素标记点，标记点颜色与所在矩形的边框颜色不同，但同一矩形内所有标记点颜色相同。不同矩形内的标记点颜色各不相同。矩形之间不重叠、不相邻。\\n- `Rule`：对每个闭合矩形边框，找到其内部所有标记点的颜色（同一矩形内标记点颜色唯一）。将该矩形的整条边框重绘为标记点的颜色，同时将所有标记点的像素替换为该矩形原来的边框颜色。背景像素保持不变。\\n- `Key insight`：边框颜色和内部标记点颜色发生互换——解题者需要先识别每个封闭边框与其内部标记点之间的配对关系，再执行颜色交换。表面看似简单的颜色替换，关键在于正确判定\\\"哪些标记点属于哪个边框\\\"这一归属关系。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：将网格中每个多色精灵按其内部颜色层数进行\\\"剥洋葱\\\"式分解，从外到内逐层提取轮廓并按从左到右的顺序排列在输出网格中。\\n- `Input structure`：背景为 black。网格中有若干个独立的多色精灵（互不接触），每个精灵由 2 到 4 种颜色组成，呈同心嵌套结构——最外层是一种颜色，向内每层换一种颜色，类似靶心图案（但形状不一定是矩形，可以是不规则的 4-连通区域，只要每层完整包裹内层即可）。每个精灵的层数可能不同。\\n- `Rule`：对每个精灵，从最外层开始逐层\\\"剥离\\\"——第一层是精灵最外圈像素构成的轮廓（即与背景 4-连通相邻的像素），第二层是去掉最外层后新暴露的外圈像素，依此类推，直到最内层核心。将每一层单独提取出来（保持其相对空间位置），按照从外到内的顺序从左到右排列在输出网格中，层与层之间用一列背景色分隔。每层只保留该层自身颜色的像素，其余位置为背景色。精灵之间的排列顺序按照它们在输入网格中从上到下、从左到右的出现顺序，精灵之间用两列背景色分隔。\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先识别每个精灵的同心嵌套层级结构，再理解\\\"剥离\\\"的顺序是从外向内逐层提取轮廓。两个非显然的推理步骤：（1）判断哪些像素属于同一\\\"层\\\"（即当前最外圈），（2）理解输出中各层的排列顺序编码了原精灵的嵌套深度。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：在网格中找到由墙壁围成的若干房间，每个房间有一个彩色钥匙和一扇同色的门（墙壁缺口），将钥匙颜色填充到连接钥匙所在房间与同色门所在房间之间的走廊中。\\n- `Input structure`：背景为 black。grey 像素构成正交墙壁，将网格分隔成若干矩形房间和连接房间的窄走廊（宽度为 1 格）。每个房间内恰好有一个彩色单像素（钥匙），颜色各不相同（可能有 red、blue、green、yellow 等）。每个房间的墙壁上恰好有一个缺口（宽度 1 格），缺口处有一个与某个钥匙同色的像素（门）。钥匙颜色与其所在房间的门颜色不同，但与另一个房间的门颜色相同。走廊只有 black 像素，连接各个房间的缺口。\\n- `Rule`：（1）匹配：每把钥匙与同色的门配对。（2）路径填充：从钥匙所在房间的缺口出发，沿走廊找到通向配对门所在房间的唯一路径（走廊网络中任意两个房间之间只有唯一路径，即树状拓扑）。将该走廊路径上的所有 black 像素填充为钥匙的颜色。（3）钥匙原位置设为 black，门像素保持不变，墙壁保持不变，房间内部其余位置保持不变。\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要完成两层推理：首先通过颜色匹配建立钥匙-门的配对关系（钥匙不在自己门所在的房间里，而在另一个房间），然后理解走廊路径的填充规则——走廊是树状结构所以路径唯一。颜色匹配是跨房间的间接关联，走廊路径填充则需要识别墙壁定义的拓扑连接结构。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：网格中有若干形状各异的单色精灵，每个精灵旁边有一个由相同颜色绘制的小 L 形箭头指示翻转方式；将每个精灵按箭头编码的轴进行镜像翻转。\\n- `Input structure`：背景为主色调（如 azure）。网格中有若干 4-连通的单色精灵，每个精灵的颜色互不相同。每个精灵的某一侧（上、下、左或右）紧邻一个由同色像素组成的 3 像素 L 形箭头标记——箭头由一条 2 像素长的直线段加上末端垂直拐弯的 1 像素构成，直线段的一端紧贴精灵边缘，另一端的拐弯像素向某个方向偏移。L 形标记与精灵之间无间隔（直接 4-连通相邻），且 L 形标记不与精灵的主体像素混淆（精灵主体像素数量至少为 5，L 形恰好 3 像素，且 L 形可通过其形状被唯一识别）。\\n- `Rule`：对每个精灵：（1）识别与精灵相邻的 L 形标记。L 形标记由 3 个同色像素组成，形成直角拐弯。（2）根据 L 形标记的朝向确定翻转轴——如果 L 形的拐弯像素相对于直线段在水平方向上偏移（即 L 形开口朝左或朝右），则执行左右镜像翻转（沿精灵竖直中轴翻转）；如果在垂直方向上偏移（即 L 形开口朝上或朝下），则执行上下镜像翻转（沿精灵水平中轴翻转）。（3）将精灵相对于自身包围盒中心执行对应的镜像翻转，翻转后位置不变。（4）删除 L 形标记（设为背景色）。背景保持不变。\\n- `Key insight`：解题者面临两层推理挑战：第一层是将 3 像素的 L 形从精灵主体中区分出来并解读其编码方式——L 形的开口方向并非指示移动方向，而是编码翻转轴的类型；第二层是正确执行精灵的原位镜像翻转。箭头编码方式的隐蔽性是本题的核心难点。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：网格被分割线分成四个面板，四个面板中的图案互补拼合为一个完整图案，同时每个面板角落的颜色提示块定义了一个跨面板的颜色重映射关系，输出为按此映射着色的完整拼合图案。\\n- `Input structure`：背景为 black。网格由 grey 的单像素宽分割线划分成 2×2 共四个大小相同的面板。四个面板共享同一个底层图案，但每个面板只显示该图案的一部分（即图案中的部分像素被擦除为背景色），且四个面板的可见部分互补——将四个面板叠加后恰好能恢复完整图案，任何像素位置至多在一个面板中可见。每个面板的可见像素全部是同一种颜色（如 red、blue、green、yellow，四个面板四种不同颜色）。此外，在每个面板的右下角有一个 1×1 的颜色提示块，其颜色等于另一个面板的可见像素颜色（四个提示块构成一个一一映射，无自映射）。\\n- `Rule`：（1）将四个面板的可见图案叠加，恢复出完整图案。（2）建立颜色映射：如果面板 A 的提示块颜色等于面板 B 的可见像素颜色，则在输出中，面板 B 贡献的所有像素用面板 A 的可见像素颜色绘制。（3）输出为单个面板大小的网格，包含完整图案，每个像素按上述映射着色。背景像素保持 black。提示块本身不出现在输出中。\\n- `Key insight`：本题包含三层推理：第一层是发现四个面板的图案互补，可以拼成一个完整图案；第二层是理解右下角提示块建立了面板间的颜色映射关系；第三层是正确应用这个映射——提示块指定的是\\\"谁的像素在输出中用我的颜色\\\"这一间接重定向关系。跨面板的间接颜色映射构成了本题的核心挑战。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：将网格中散布的碎片精灵按照边缘锯齿形状配对拼合成完整矩形，拼合后矩形内部的条纹方向决定该矩形在输出中是否旋转。\\n- `Input structure`：背景为 black。网格中有若干单色的不规则精灵，每个精灵的一侧边缘呈锯齿状（凹凸交替，凹凸深度为 1 像素），其余三侧边缘为直线。精灵颜色有若干种，每种颜色恰好有两个精灵。同色的两个精灵锯齿边缘互补——一个的凸出恰好填入另一个的凹陷，拼合后形成一个完整的矩形。每个精灵内部有 1 到 3 条平行的 grey 细线条纹（宽度 1 像素），条纹方向为水平或垂直，同一精灵内条纹方向一致。\\n- `Rule`：（1）按颜色配对精灵，将同色的两个精灵沿锯齿边缘拼合成一个完整矩形（通过平移使锯齿互补对齐，锯齿边缘相对放置）。（2）观察拼合后矩形内部 grey 条纹的方向：如果条纹是水平的，矩形保持原样不旋转；如果条纹是垂直的，将整个矩形顺时针旋转 90 度。（3）将所有拼合并可能旋转后的矩形按面积从小到大、从左到右排列在输出网格中，矩形之间用一列 black 分隔，底部对齐。grey 条纹在输出中保留。\\n- `Key insight`：本题有两层核心推理：第一层是通过锯齿边缘的互补形状识别配对关系并完成拼合——解题者需要发现同色精灵的锯齿边缘恰好吻合；第二层是发现内部条纹方向编码了旋转指令，条纹不是装饰而是操作信号。拼合机制与旋转编码的结合使得解题路径具有层次感。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：网格中的彩色连通区域各自包含一个异色\\\"种子\\\"像素，种子的颜色编码了生长方向；每个区域沿对应方向扩展边界直到受阻。\\n- `Input structure`：背景为 black。网格中有若干 4-连通的单色区域（颜色各不相同，可能包括 red、blue、green、yellow 等），区域之间互不接触，至少间隔 2 格背景。每个区域内部恰好有一个像素颜色与区域主色不同，这是\\\"种子\\\"像素。种子像素的颜色只会是以下四种之一：orange 表示向右生长、magenta 表示向下生长、azure 表示向左生长、maroon 表示向上生长。同一种种子颜色可以出现在多个区域中。\\n- `Rule`：（1）确定每个区域的种子颜色，对应生长方向：orange→右、magenta→下、azure→左、maroon→上。（2）将该区域沿指定方向逐列（或逐行）扩展：每次在区域朝该方向的整条边界外侧添加一列/行像素（颜色为区域主色）。（3）重复扩展，直到新添加的像素会与另一个区域的像素 4-连通相邻或触及网格边缘时停止（停在碰撞前一步，不添加会导致碰撞的那一列/行）。（4）种子像素在输出中被替换为区域主色（种子标记消失）。所有区域的扩展终止位置基于它们各自独立扩展到极限后的状态同时计算，不存在顺序依赖。\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要解决两层推理问题：第一层是建立种子颜色到生长方向的映射（需要从多个样例中归纳出四种种子颜色分别对应哪个方向，这不是直觉上显然的对应关系）；第二层是理解生长的机制——区域沿单一方向整列/行扩展直到受阻，且所有区域的扩展是同时判定的。种子颜色编码方向的映射关系需要跨样例归纳，是本题的核心隐蔽规律。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210621_gpt54_high_missing/12__codegen_prompts__6.log:34:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '/\\\"'^def main(/,/''^def /p'\\\"' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/e8686506.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Assemble scattered colored fragments into a left-right symmetric rectangle, jigsaw-style.\\n\\n    Input structure:\\n    - bg = most common color; remaining colors form small sprite fragments.\\n    - Optional roles: 4 singleton pixels of one color mark corners; horizontal bars mark top/bottom edges; paired vertical lines mark left/right edges.\\n\\n    Rule:\\n    - Collect all non-bg connected components as jigsaw pieces.\\n    - Determine output rectangle dimensions from total piece area.\\n    - Pack pieces into the rectangle so it is exactly mirror-symmetric (left-right) and same-color pieces never 4-touch.\\n\\n    Key insight: Left-right symmetry plus the no-same-color-touching constraint make the assembly unique; corner/edge markers anchor it when present.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\n    bg = get_bg(g)\\n\\n    # Extract pieces (connected components per color)\\n    comps_by_color: dict[int, list[list[tuple[int, int]]]] = {}\\n    pieces = []\\n    color_piece_count: dict[int, int] = {}\\n\\n    for col in sorted(set(map(int, np.unique(g)))):\\n        if col == bg:\\n            continue\\n        comps = components_mask(g == col, connectivity=4)\\n        comps_by_color[col] = comps\\n        color_piece_count[col] = len(comps)\\n        for pts in comps:\\n            _, _, coords = _piece_sig(pts)\\n            pieces.append((col, coords))\\n\\n    # Group identical pieces into types\\n    from collections import Counter\\n\\n    ctr = Counter(pieces)\\n    types = []\\n    for (col, coords), cnt in sorted(ctr.items(), key=lambda kv: (-len(kv[0][1]), kv[0][0], kv[0][1])):\\n        arr = np.array(coords, dtype=int)\\n        h = int(arr[:, 0].max() + 1)\\n        w = int(arr[:, 1].max() + 1)\\n        types.append({\\\"col\\\": int(col), \\\"coords\\\": coords, \\\"h\\\": h, \\\"w\\\": w, \\\"cnt\\\": int(cnt)})\\n\\n    total_area = sum(int(t[\\\"cnt\\\"]) * len(t[\\\"coords\\\"]) for t in types)\\n    assert total_area > 0, \\\"total_area must be positive: grid must contain non-background pieces\\\"\\n\\n    # Disallow 4-neigh touching between different pieces of same color (preserve component counts)\\n    # Eval inputs use the unique closest-to-square portrait factor pair as the output shape.\\n    dims = [(h, w) for (h, w) in _factors(total_area) if h >= w]\\n    assert dims, \\\"at least one portrait factor pair must exist for the total piece area\\\"\\n    best_gap = min(abs(h - w) for h, w in dims)\\n    best_dims = [(h, w) for h, w in dims if abs(h - w) == best_gap]\\n    assert len(best_dims) == 1, \\\"closest-to-square portrait output shape must be unique\\\"\\n    H, W = best_dims[0]\\n\\n    # Frame constraint: under 8-connectivity, 1-2 pieces must exist whose union bbox\\n    # equals the output rectangle (H x W). Their relative positions are fixed in output.\\n    comps8_all = []\\n    for col in sorted(set(map(int, np.unique(g))) - {bg}):\\n        for pts in components_mask(g == col, connectivity=8):\\n            comps8_all.append((int(col), pts))\\n    def _is_lr_symmetric(parts, h, w):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Check if the union of frame parts forms an LR-symmetric bitmap.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        all_pts = np.concatenate([p for _, p in parts])\\n        r0, c0 = int(all_pts[:, 0].min()), int(all_pts[:, 1].min())\\n        bmp = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=bool)\\n        for _, pts in parts:\\n            for r, c in pts:\\n                bmp[int(r) - r0, int(c) - c0] = True\\n        return np.array_equal(bmp, bmp[:, ::-1])\\n\\n    frame_parts: list[tuple[int, np.ndarray]] = []\\n    for i, (c1, p1) in enumerate(comps8_all):\\n        r0, c0, r1, c1b = bbox_coords(p1)\\n        if r1 - r0 + 1 == H and c1b - c0 + 1 == W:\\n            if _is_lr_symmetric([(c1, p1)], H, W):\\n                frame_parts = [(c1, p1)]\\n                break\\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(comps8_all)):\\n            c2, p2 = comps8_all[j]\\n            union = np.concatenate([p1, p2])\\n            ur0, uc0, ur1, uc1 = bbox_coords(union)\\n            if ur1 - ur0 + 1 == H and uc1 - uc0 + 1 == W:\\n                if _is_lr_symmetric([(c1, p1), (c2, p2)], H, W):\\n                    frame_parts = [(c1, p1), (c2, p2)]\\n                    break\\n        if frame_parts:\\n            break\\n    assert frame_parts, \\\"input must contain 1-2 LR-symmetric pieces (8-conn) whose union bbox equals output dims\\\"\\n\\n    req = _build_requirements(H, W, comps_by_color)\\n\\n    # Lock frame cells into req: their output positions are determined by input-relative positions.\\n    all_frame_pts = np.concatenate([p for _, p in frame_parts])\\n    fr0, fc0 = int(all_frame_pts[:, 0].min()), int(all_frame_pts[:, 1].min())\\n    for col, pts in frame_parts:\\n        for r, c in pts:\\n            or_, oc = int(r) - fr0, int(c) - fc0\\n            if 0 <= or_ < H and 0 <= oc < W:\\n                req[or_, oc] = col\\n\\n    disallow_touch = {col for col, n in color_piece_count.items() if n > 1}\\n    sol = _assemble(types, H, W, req, disallow_touch)\\n    return sol.astype(int)\\n\\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\\n\\n# === CFG: Output dimensions ===\\n_AREA_MIN = 25               # minimum total piece area\\n_AREA_MAX = 50               # maximum total piece area (exclusive upper in range)\\n_WIDTH_REQUIRED = 5           # all valid outputs have width 5\\n_HEIGHT_MAX = 10              # maximum output height\\n\\n# === CFG: Color and palette ===\\n_N_COLORS_MIN = 4             # min distinct colors in abstract output\\n_N_COLORS_MAX = 6             # max distinct colors in abstract output\\n_TWO_FRAME_MIN_H = 6          # min height to allow 2-color frame\\n_TWO_FRAME_MIN_COLORS = 5     # min palette size to allow 2-color frame\\n_TWO_FRAME_PROB = 0.35         # probability of splitting frame into 2 colors\\n_CENTER_CAP_PROB = 0.5         # probability of capping center col at top/bottom\\n\\n# === CFG: Piece constraints ===\\n_MAX_PIECE_AREA = 6           # maximum area of any single 4-conn piece\\n_MAX_CHUNK_SIZE = 6           # max cells per hole chunk when splitting large holes\\n_PIECE_COUNT_MIN = 9          # min total 4-conn components in output\\n_PIECE_COUNT_MAX = 17         # max total 4-conn components in output\\n\\n# === CFG: Canvas / scatter ===\\n_CANVAS_MIN = 13              # min canvas dimension (rows and cols)\\n_CANVAS_MAX = 15              # max canvas dimension (rows and cols)\\n_SCATTER_PADDING = 1          # Chebyshev padding between scattered pieces\\n\\n# === CFG: Retry ===\\n_GEN_MAX_RETRIES = 300        # max attempts in generate_input()\\n\\n\\ndef _valid_dims():\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210621_gpt54_high_missing/12__codegen_prompts__6.log:52:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_22\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"实现计划：\\n1. 写一套最小自包含几何 helper：连通域、裁剪、平移拼接、矩形满铺检测。\\n2. `main()` 先按非黑连通域取碎片，再按主色配对；每对碎片用平移枚举寻找唯一的“无重叠且并集恰好是完整矩形”的装配结果。\\n3. 在装配后的矩形里读 grey 条纹方向，必要时顺时针旋转，再按面积升序和输入中的左到右顺序做底对齐排版。\\n4. `generate_input()` 随机生成 2-4 组矩形，覆盖纵向/横向锯齿切分、横/竖条纹、1-3 条纹、不同尺寸和散布位置；用重试保证不粘连、不退化、输出不超 30。\\n5. 写完立即跑题目给的 100 次自检和 `py_compile`，再清理 `__pycache__`。\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/